/exception-track/1794387514000-js-r1r3-round-record.md:82:1. `js-retained-condition-retention-and-lookup` (owner: yang.typescript; raised by sol at\ncollab/exception-track/1794387514000-js-r1r3-round-record.md:89:3. Track end-gates unchanged: 12-directed-pair matrix, host-by-VM portability beyond the\ncollab/exception-track/1794362000000-engineer-r4-equivalence-proof.prompt.md:26:port brief. Your job is to make the failure IMPOSSIBLE to miss if it exists, not to make\ncollab/exception-track/1794362000000-engineer-r4-equivalence-proof.prompt.md:40:1. **Static intra-unit packet call** — `dsg__intra_call` → `call-entry` vector branch\ncollab/exception-track/1794362000000-engineer-r4-equivalence-proof.prompt.md:59:- **Retention security (owner decision 2026-11-11: VM seam DECLINED; decisive)**: the protocol-condition carrier is the WITNESS mechanism (contents in a guest-admissible cell), whose known limitation is replay/mutation — a guest may `cell/set!` a caught wrapper's contents or copy them into a fresh cell. The proof must test exactly astra's replay/mutation probes across the three lanes AND state whether the continuation lane closes them (it is expected to: under raise-exit semantics there is no retention object at all). If the outcome channel cannot match the continuation lane here, that IS the equivalence failure and the (B) fallback triggers under the owner's standing authorization.\ncollab/exception-track/1794362000000-engineer-r4-equivalence-proof.prompt.md:62:  (b) `clojure→python→clojure`. Prove `dsg__admitted?` and `:clj/outcomes?` cannot\ncollab/exception-track/1794362000000-engineer-r4-equivalence-proof.prompt.md:63:  disagree when the callee's `dsg__call_token` was minted in a different unit\ncollab/exception-track/1794362000000-engineer-r4-equivalence-proof.prompt.md:79:## Report\ncollab/exception-track/1794370000000-engineer-r3-glmsplit-implementation.prompt.md:12:1. `collab/exception-track/1794369000000-mob-record-r3-retention-design.md` — the mob r