ling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:7:`git grep -n 'dsg__condition' 98519957` finds **11 lines across 9 sites**, all in [`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) (`0` occurrences on `master` @ `8cd9fc92`, `0` occurrences in `test/`):\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:11:1. **[`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1543-1544`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1543-L1544)** — [`condition->outcome`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1530-L1549) inside [`compile-guest-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1517-L1658) (consequent branch when `reason` is one of `:yang.call/{thrown, not-callable, invalid-invocation, unsupported-binding}`):\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:14:                 (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v condition) (u/lit :dsg__condition) (u/lit true)))\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:19:                 (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc)\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:21:                        (u/lit :dsg__condition) (u/lit true)))\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:23:3. **[`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1560-1567`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1560-L1567)** — `refused` inside [`compile-guest-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1517-L1658) (when `(dsg__admitted? callee)` is false):\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:24:   stamps `(u/lit :dsg__condition) (u/lit true)` onto `(yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable {:yang.call/callee callee})`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:26:   stamps `(u/lit :dsg__condition) (u/lit true)` onto `(yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit})`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:27:5. **[`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1630-1636`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1630-L1636)** — `value-call` inside [`compile-guest-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1517-L1658) (when `dsg__raise_escape` fails `:clj/escape-token` check):\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:28:   stamps `(u/lit :dsg__condition) (u/lit true)` onto `(yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit})`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:29:6. **[`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2612-2617`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2612-L2617)** — `dsg__intra_call` inside [`compile-program`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2398-L2678) (non-map `dsg__callee` branch):\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:32:          (dsg__assoc (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:33:                                           (dsg__assoc {} :yang.call/callee dsg__callee))\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:34:                      :dsg__condition true))\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:40:                 :dsg__condition true))\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:46:   When a callable activation finishes with `outcome = [:yin.k/error err-val]`, tests `(if (data/map? err-val) (dsg__get err-val :dsg__condition) false)`:\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:47:   - **Truthy**: calls `(u/app raise (u/app (u/v 'data/dissoc) (u/v err-val) (u/lit :dsg__condition)))` — strips `:dsg__condition` and forwards `err-val` directly as the condition to `raise`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:50:   Wraps `(go forms initial-macro-env)` in `(u/let1 top-res ast ...)`; when `(= (data/nth top-res 0) :yin.k/error)` and `(dsg__get top-err :dsg__condition)` is truthy, returns `[:yin.k/error (data/dissoc top-err :dsg__condition)]`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:54:### 2. Why `test-value-invocation-refusals-are-terminating` (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2598`) and the R3 Tests Failed with `:dsg__condition true`\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:59:2. `invoke-value` ([`clojure.cljc:2794-2795`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2794-L2795)) throws `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable, :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee 5}, :dsg__condition true}`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:60:3. `invoke-value`'s [`call-entry`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1312-L1315) strips `:dsg__condition` and passes `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable, :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee 5}}` to `value-call`'s `:yang.call/raise` handler ([`clojure.cljc:1617-1622`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1617-L1622)).\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:61:4. `value-call`'s `:yang.call/raise` handler invokes [`condition->outcome`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1543-L1544), which **re-stamps `:dsg__condition true`** and escapes via `dsg__raise_escape` with `[:yin.k/error {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable, :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee 5}, :dsg__condition true}]`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:65:   - Next, [`strip-top-outcome`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2507) wraps `(go forms initial-macro-env)` as the **operand** (`ast`) of `(u/let1 top-res ast ...)` (`((fn [top-res] ...) ast)`).\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:67:   - On `:walker` (which ignores `:tail?`), `ast` returns normally into `strip-top-outcome`, which strips `:dsg__condition`. On `:semantic` ([`yin.vm.semantic.linearize:116`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L116)), the stale `:tail? true` on `ast` emits a tail `:call` (`tail? = true`) that returns directly out of the enclosing frame, **bypassing `strip-top-outcome` completely**.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:71:### 3. Why **(B) Load-bearing** Holds (Why Simply Deleting `:dsg__condition` Fails R3 + R5)\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:81:- Furthermore, because [`check-program-symbols!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2370-L2394) rejects reserved-prefix **symbols** (`symbol?` at `:2377`, `:2386`) and **not keywords**, guest source can legally write `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable, :dsg__condition true}`. Checking `(dsg__get err-val :dsg__condition)` for literal `true` allows guest code to forge a retained condition, violating **Ruling v2 §R5** (*\"forged or source-writable attributes on a wrapper-looking value never authenticate a retained condition\"*).\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:90:   - At [`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2674`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2674), replace `u/mark-tails` with [`yang.tails/remark-tails`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/tails.cljc#L72-L77) (or pass `(if (outcomes? env) false tail?)` to `go` at [`:2446`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2446) in addition to `remark-tails`), so pre-existing `:tail? true` marks inside `(go forms initial-macro-env)` are stripped and recomputed after `strip-top-outcome` wraps the body at [`:2507`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2507).\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:91:2. **Authenticate `:dsg__condition` with the compiler-held closure token `dsg__call_token` instead of literal `true` (satisfying R5)**:\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:92:   - `dsg__call_token` ([`clojure.cljc:2632`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2632)) is already an unforgeable per-unit closure value (`(fn [x] x)`) in scope of `call-entry`, `compile-guest-call`, `dsg__intra_call`, and `strip-top-outcome`, and its symbol name `dsg__call_token` is blocked in user forms by [`check-program-symbols!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2370-L2394).\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:93:   - At writer sites **#1–#6** ([`clojure.cljc:1544, 1548, 1567, 1586, 1636, 2617`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1543-L1636)), stamp `:dsg__condition` with `(u/v 'dsg__call_token)` (and `dsg__call_token` in quoted `dsg__intra_call` at `:2617`) instead of `true`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:94:   - At writer site **#7** (`invoke-value` in `library`, [`clojure.cljc:2794-2795`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2794-L2795)), remove `(throw (assoc ... :dsg__condition true))` and instead trigger a genuine `not-callable` refusal that stamps `dsg__call_token` via compiler-generated code (or invoke `(f)` / a non-callable refusal helper lowered by the compiler), because `library` forms pass through `check-program-symbols!` when spliced in `run-library` tests.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:95:   - At the two reader/stripper sites ([`call-entry` at `clojure.cljc:1312-1315`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1312-L1315) and [`strip-top-outcome` at `clojure.cljc:2430-2433`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2430-L2433)), replace the truthiness check `(dsg__get err-val :dsg__condition)` with token equality `(dsg__equal (dsg__get err-val :dsg__condition) dsg__call_token)`.\ncollab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:96:   - Thus, the external wire condition map leaving `call-entry` (`raise`) or leaving the top-level program (`strip-top-outcome`) is strictly `{:yang.call/reason <kw>, :yang.call/data <map>}` (or `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value <val>}`) with `:dsg__condition` stripped, while inside `try`/`catch` the retained condition carries `:dsg__condition dsg__call_token` so an unchanged `(throw e)` (immediate or delayed via `retain`/`later`) is recognized by