{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md; nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794400000000-engineer-port-clojure-continuations.prompt.md; rg -n -A 35 -B 8 'S2|replay|mutation|reserved' docs/agents/known-gaps.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-07 04:30:00 GMT\n     2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-07 11:30:00 +07 (+0700)\n     3\tStatus: OWNER-APPROVED 2026-11-07 (\"enforce everywhere consistently. this should be a separate track.\"); v2 SUPERSEDES v1 (1794920000000) per the review round — architect gpt-6-astra, engineer mob gpt-6.1-sol + gemini-3.8-flash: all three ACCEPT WITH AMENDMENTS, folded below. Qwen aborted (headless tool denial); kimi quota-exhausted (429).\n     4\tReview records: collab/exception-track/1794930000000-architect-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log, 1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log, 1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gemini-3.8-flash.stdout.log.\n     5\t\n     6\t# RULING OF RECORD v2 — the exception track: §8.10.7 enforced uniformly in all four frontends\n     7\t\n     8\t## The decision\n     9\t\n    10\tException handling is enforced uniformly across yang.clojure, yang.typescript (js),\n    11\tyang.php, and yang.python. At every admitted guest-call boundary, an escaping source\n    12\texception compiles down to THE SAME continuation: the caller's supplied raise exit\n    13\treceiving the §8.10.7 condition\n    14\t\n    15\t    {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value original-thrown-value}\n    16\t\n    17\tand every receiving runtime implements the §8.10.7 reception rules as written. This is a\n    18\tSEPARATE TRACK: its own folder (collab/exception-track/), its own rounds, its own\n    19\tacceptance gate; the four frontend seats cede the exception-fix surfaces to the track and\n    20\treceive per-frontend results back into their records.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Scope bounds (v2: sharpened per astra §5)\n    23\t\n    24\t- \"Every boundary\" means ADMITTED GUEST-CALL boundaries. VM/custody defects and host\n    25\t  implementation failures remain operational failures (design :3904); no broad\n    26\t  host catch-and-relabel is authorized.\n    27\t- A RETURNED condition-shaped map is ordinary data; a THROWN condition-shaped map is the\n    28\t  payload of a fresh condition; shape is never evidence of an existing condition to\n    29\t  forward (the cell-ref rule, restated — R5).\n    30\t- \"Same continuation\" does NOT require identical internal lowering (R4's allowance).\n    31\t\n    32\t## The requirements (v2: amended per the review round)\n    33\t\n    34\t**R1 — the callee bridge (js AND php non-compliant today).** Every frontend's published\n    35\tfunction entry, closure entry, and higher-order entry installs the exception bridge\n    36\tBEFORE argument binding: it reads the supplied `:yang.call/raise` and delivers every\n    37\tescaping source exception AND argument-binding failure to it as the thrown condition,\n    38\texactly once, with execution after the call unreachable. js entries apply `:code` without\n    39\treading the raise exit (prelude.cljc:1581); php's function entry (:2264) and Closure entry\n    40\t(:4217) lack it, and php's raise with an empty handler stack RETURNS normally\n    41\t(prelude.cljc:194-197). The bridge must also satisfy §8.10.8: complete cleanup and\n    42\thandler/depth/frame restoration BEFORE the transfer; a later generator resume never\n    43\treuses a raise exit belonging to a completed call.\n    44\t\n    45\t**R2 — foreign reception and retained-condition lifetime (python, php non-compliant\n    46\ttoday).** On receiving a thrown condition: (1) a payload valid in the receiving runtime\n    47\tkeeps its ordinary catching and identity behavior — delivered UNCHANGED (python raising\n    48\tan already-local exception raw is compliant; python raising an OTHERWISE-FOREIGN payload\n    49\traw at :1034 is not); (2) js may deliver the otherwise-foreign payload raw; (3) python\n    50\tand php represent an otherwise-foreign payload with their own generated\n    51\t`ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original payload — catch-all\n    52\tcatches it, typed catches match the LOCAL hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names,\n    53\tand formatting it never implicitly invokes foreign methods. Retention rides the generated\n    54\texception's IDENTITY for its ENTIRE LIFETIME, outside source-writable attributes, with no\n    55\tambient registry (design :3878, :3885). Raising the whole envelope (php :2384) or an\n    56\totherwise-foreign raw payload (python :1034) is non-compliant.\n    57\t\n    58\t**R3 — protocol failures retain and forward the condition (ALL FOUR frontends; v2\n    59\twidened per astra §1 / sol §1).** `:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`,\n    60\t`:yang.call/unsupported-binding` (fully qualified) map to a documented local exception\n    61\tform retaining the complete original condition — qualified reason AND plain evidence — so\n    62\tan unchanged rethrow FORWARDS the original condition without a new wrapper. js discards\n    63\tthe condition into fresh text (:1627); python builds a generic TypeError (:1046); clojure\n    64\tretains it as catch data (:1306) but public escape reclassifies through unconditional\n    65\t`yang.call/thrown` (:1088); php constructs a fresh Error for not-callable and raises the\n    66\tenvelope otherwise (:2384), and its source rethrow rejects that envelope (:4085). All\n    67\tfour are in scope, reception AND outbound rethrow.\n    68\t\n    69\t**R4 — clojure unifies or proves equivalence.** The intra-unit outcome-token channel\n    70\t(clojure.cljc:1115, :1125-1133) may remain an optimization only with equivalence proof\n    71\tacross caught/uncaught throws, protocol rethrow, binding failures, and higher-order\n    72\tre-entry (§8.10.9's bar) — a single passing example is insufficient. Public\n    73\tprotocol-rethrow repair (R3) does not wait for this decision. Clojure's restricted catch\n    74\tsurface (single catch, no `finally`) is a source-semantics decision this ruling does not\n    75\tchange.\n    76\t\n    77\t**R5 — no new shape-routing.** Per the scope bounds above; plus: forged or\n    78\tsource-writable attributes on a wrapper-looking value never authenticate a retained\n    79\tcondition.\n    80\t\n    81\t## The baseline (audit of record)\n    82\t\n    83\tThe gpt-6.1-sol audit (collab/yang-python/1794900000000, verdict DIVERGENT, HEAD\n    84\te9a0b430) is the baseline. Citation corrections of record from the review round: js\n    85\tfollows its GUEST continuation handler stack (js.rt/ctx, prelude.cljc:1704), not the host\n    86\tengine's; php's empty-stack return is :194-197 (envelope reception :2384); clojure's\n    87\tactual private branches are :1115 and :1125-1133 (:1110 is the packet-length guard).\n    88\t\n    89\t## Acceptance gate (v2: widened per astra §4 / sol §4)\n    90\t\n    91\tThe track is DONE when ALL of the following hold, with real source on both sides of every\n    92\tleg:\n    93\t\n    94\t1. **The directed pair matrix — 12 cross-language directions** derived from the four\n    95\t   admitted frontends (clojure↔python and clojure↔php explicitly included), plus local\n    96\t   regressions.\n    97\t2. **Callable-kind coverage**: named exports AND closure/higher-order entries (php\n    98\t   Closures concretely), supported methods/callable objects per frontend capability.\n    99\t3. **The §8.10.11 exception scenarios**: binding failures; arbitrary foreign thrown\n   100\t   data; catch-all and typed catches (where the source has them — js has no typed-catch\n   101\t   syntax, clojure's admitted surface rejects `finally`; exercise cleanup in a frontend\n   102\t   that supports it and PRESERVE clojure's rejection tests); unchanged rethrow; finally\n   103\t   replacement; protocol-error rethrow; condition-shaped thrown maps staying data;\n   104\t   A→B→A propagation asserting original identity and cleanup order; the stored\n   105\t   ForeignException rethrown from another activation.\n   106\t4. **Context lifetime**: repeated success→raise→success, cross-runtime recursion,\n   107\t   suspension/resume — handler/depth/frame state restored, exactly-once\n   108\t   binding/cleanup.\n   109\t5. **Host-by-VM results**: JVM, Node, and Dart across the admitted VM paths, with\n   110\t   explicit refusals; portable parser-produced fixtures where the JVM-only kit cannot\n   111\t   reach; bundled-walker paths where admitted, never requiring unsupported linked\n   112\t   execution; bundled/linked parity and task isolation preserving existing custody\n   113\t   refusals.\n   114\t6. **Identity assertions BEFORE rendering**: original reasons, complete evidence, payload\n   115\t   identity, wrapper non-stacking, cleanup order — equal rendered text is not identity\n   116\t   evidence.\n   117\t\n   118\t## Sequencing (v2: corrected per astra §3 / sol §3 — the v1 order is REJECTED)\n   119\t\n   120\t0. Contract + focused FAILING fixtures first (retained-condition provenance; boundary\n   121\t   fixtures construct malformed invocations source cannot naturally build).\n   122\t1. **JS R1 + R3** together (R3 alone cannot cross the boundary while entries ignore the\n   123\t   exit).\n   124\t2. **PHP R1 + R2 + R3 as ONE coherent round** — function entry, Closure entry, and all\n   125\t   three call helpers (php/call, call-with-binding-profile, call-named). Landing the\n   126\t   bridge before reception repair would route local Throwables into the envelope-raising\n   127\t   receiver and break existing local typed catches.\n   128\t3. **Python R2 + R3 with the egress change** (prelude.cljc:912's always-fresh condition\n   129\t   must become condition-preserving for retained wrappers).\n   130\t4. **Clojure R3, then R4** (the optimization decision last).\n   131\tJS and Python work proceed independently once the contract lands; no Clojure-containing\n   132\tpair declares conformance before its R3 gap closes.\n   133\t\n   134\t— filed by the yang.python orchestrator seat; owner decision 2026-11-07\n     1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-11 09:40:00 GMT\n     2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 16:40:00 +07 (+0700)\n     3\tCoding-Agent: deepseek\n     4\tSession-ID: de4f7213-1c5d-4822-aa89-a32cbfc19e9e\n     5\t# Task: engineer — THE PORT: yang.clojure exceptions converge onto the continuation encoding\n     6\tRole: Engineer (the arc's capstone round)\n     7\tImplementers:\n     8\t- Model: deepseek-v4-pro | Assigned: 2026-11-11 16:40 +0700 | Status: active | Rationale: deepest context on this file's call/entry/outcome machinery; most honest track record of the arc.\n     9\t\n    10\t## The directive\n    11\t\n    12\tOwner decision of record (read `collab/exception-track/1794372000000-owner-decision-r3-vm-retained-seam.md`,\n    13\tFINAL DIRECTIVE section): **yang.clojure's exception lowering converges onto the continuation\n    14\tencoding** — the same `%capture` handler-stack scheme as python/typescript/php. No VM change. The\n    15\toutcome model (slice-5) is retired. R4 becomes port verification.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Phase 0 — LaTTe depth harness FIRST (blocking prerequisite)\n    18\t\n    19\t`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` collects no continuation depth today (astra verified at :239).\n    20\tAdd depth collection (max live continuation depth per workload) and record pre-port baselines for\n    21\tevery corpus workload to a committed EDN file. This is the yardstick for criterion 4 below. Do not\n    22\tproceed to Phase 1 without committed baselines.\n    23\t\n    24\t## Phase 1 — the port\n    25\t\n    26\tBranch: extend `exception-r3-impl` (the §8.10.7 bridge work and the six protocol rows' bridge\n    27\tconformance carry forward; the outcome internals they were expressed through do not). Worktree\n    28\t`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch`.\n    29\t\n    30\t1. **Drop the outcome channel**: guest functions return plain values; `[:yin.k/ok|error]` wrapping,\n    31\t   `condition->outcome`, `strip-top-outcome`, `bind-outcome`, the token-lane outcome forwarding —\n    32\t   retired.\n    33\t2. **Adopt the continuation scheme** (mirror py/ts/php; the shapes are in their preludes):\n    34\t   a `clj/try` / `clj/try-finally` / `clj/throw` family over `%capture` with a handler stack in a\n    35\t   runtime cell, `clj/call-ec` for escapes, `clj/unwind-to` running finally frames. `finally`\n    36\t   becomes EXPRESSIBLE — lift the one-catch restriction and accept `finally` in portable try.\n    37\t3. **Preserve the intra-unit private tail lane** (deepseek's remedy, mob amendment 3): direct\n    38\t   intra-unit calls keep direct tail application; only published/cross-unit entries take the\n    39\t   bridge frame. No VM change — `src/cljc/yin/vm/**` must diff EMPTY against its pre-port state.\n    40\t4. **§8.10.7 boundary conformance unchanged**: the public entry bridge installs before argument\n    41\t   binding; escaping exceptions AND binding failures deliver\n    42\t   `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value v}` (or the qualified protocol\n    43\t   condition, per R1/R3) to the caller's raise exit, exactly once, with §8.10.8 cleanup first.\n    44\t   The kit's fixtures and `:expected` values are UNCHANGED — they are the acceptance instrument.\n    45\t5. **Protocol conditions**: delivered as conditions via the bridge (no retention object needed —\n    46\t   the replay/mutation limitation dies with the outcome channel).\n    47\t6. **Retire**: `:outcomes` gating, the witness/wrapper machinery, `dsg__condition_retained`,\n    48\t   `dsg__visible_of`, `dsg__condition_wrapper` — dead code once outcomes are gone.\n    49\t7. **Source semantics widen**: portable try accepts catch (including the existing\n    50\t   Exception/ExceptionInfo shape) AND finally; document the widened surface.\n    51\t\n    52\t## Phase 2 — acceptance\n    53\t\n    54\t1. `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-test` green — with these expectations moved JUSTIFIED (the\n    55\t   constant-depth pin `test-outcome-common-call-depth` breaks BY DESIGN: re-benchmark it to the\n    56\t   honest post-port semantics — constant for handler-free intra-unit chains via the private lane\n    57\t   and for loop/recur; linear across published entries — and rename/comment accordingly).\n    58\t   `test-exception-r3-astra-probes`: the seven observation probes become trivially correct (the\n    59\t   caught value IS the payload) — keep them as pins; the two VM-behavior pins die with the seam\n    60\t   (already reverted per the NO decision).\n    61\t2. `clj -M:kondo --lint` on your files — 0/0.\n    62\t3. **NEVER run `yang.call.exception-contract-test` locally.** Commit + push `exception-r3-impl`.\n    63\t   The orchestrator runs the kit + LaTTe harness on shiva (no overlay — remember js5 discipline).\n    64\t4. Report per-phase: Phase 0 baselines (workload → max depth), Phase 1 the new try family shapes\n    65\t   (file:line), retired machinery list, moved expectations each justified, commands + counts, SHA.\n    66\t\n    67\t## Escalation thresholds (mob amendment 4)\n    68\t\n    69\tThe orchestrator will measure LaTTe max-continuation-depth pre/post on shiva. If any workload\n    70\texceeds >10× baseline or 10,000 frames, the owner reviews before merge. You do not need to gate on\n    71\tthis — build to the criteria above.\n    72\t\n    73\t## Constraints\n    74\t\n    75\tFiles: `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`, `src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc` (if needed),\n    76\t`test/yang/clojure_test.clj`, `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` (+ the baselines EDN).\n    77\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/**` stays EMPTY-diff (the declined se