of`, `dsg__condition_wrapper` — dead code once outcomes are gone.\n    49\t7. **Source semantics widen**: portable try accepts catch (including the existing\n    50\t   Exception/ExceptionInfo shape) AND finally; document the widened surface.\n    51\t\n    52\t## Phase 2 — acceptance\n    53\t\n    54\t1. `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-test` green — with these expectations moved JUSTIFIED (the\n    55\t   constant-depth pin `test-outcome-common-call-depth` breaks BY DESIGN: re-benchmark it to the\n    56\t   honest post-port semantics — constant for handler-free intra-unit chains via the private lane\n    57\t   and for loop/recur; linear across published entries — and rename/comment accordingly).\n    58\t   `test-exception-r3-astra-probes`: the seven observation probes become trivially correct (the\n    59\t   caught value IS the payload) — keep them as pins; the two VM-behavior pins die with the seam\n    60\t   (already reverted per the NO decision).\n    61\t2. `clj -M:kondo --lint` on your files — 0/0.\n    62\t3. **NEVER run `yang.call.exception-contract-test` locally.** Commit + push `exception-r3-impl`.\n    63\t   The orchestrator runs the kit + LaTTe harness on shiva (no overlay — remember js5 discipline).\n    64\t4. Report per-phase: Phase 0 baselines (workload → max depth), Phase 1 the new try family shapes\n    65\t   (file:line), retired machinery list, moved expectations each justified, commands + counts, SHA.\n    66\t\n    67\t## Escalation thresholds (mob amendment 4)\n    68\t\n    69\tThe orchestrator will measure LaTTe max-continuation-depth pre/post on shiva. If any workload\n    70\texceeds >10× baseline or 10,000 frames, the owner reviews before merge. You do not need to gate on\n    71\tthis — build to the criteria above.\n    72\t\n    73\t## Constraints\n    74\t\n    75\tFiles: `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`, `src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc` (if needed),\n    76\t`test/yang/clojure_test.clj`, `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` (+ the baselines EDN).\n    77\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/**` stays EMPTY-diff (the declined seam stays declined).\n    78\tForeground only; no background server tasks; no suite-scale local runs.\n    79\t\n    80\tBegin the final response with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local; end with the SHA and one line:\n    81\t**PORT LANDED** or **PORT BLOCKED: <what>**.\n118:| yang.php: member calls go through one `php/method-call` seam (`getMessage`, `getCode`, `getPrevious` on Throwable; `bindTo`, `__invoke` on Closure); `bindTo` shares statics with the source closure (PHP copies them); `new` and classes are refused; the call protocol validates a named argument's name at entry, so in `f(1, z: 2, w: side())` `side()` runs where PHP stops at `z` (C28, `G-method-seam`); fixture `:call-unknown-named-later-arg-runs` (oracle-only, pending) | Stage 0 gate D5 and section 3; `e2e-test/gate-fix-programs-test` | yang.php | P4 S2 (class model) and P4 S4 (`pcall-begin/arg/enter` with `new`) | P2 |\n220:| yang.php: member calls go through one `php/method-call` seam (`getMessage`, `getCode`, `getPrevious` on Throwable; `bindTo`, `__invoke` on Closure); `bindTo` shares statics with the source closure (PHP copies them); `new` and classes are refused; the call protocol validates a named argument's name at entry, so in `f(1, z: 2, w: side())` `side()` runs where PHP stops at `z` (C28, `G-method-seam`); fixture `:call-unknown-named-later-arg-runs` (oracle-only, pending) | Stage 0 gate D5 and section 3; `e2e-test/gate-fix-programs-test` | yang.php | P4 S2 (class model) and P4 S4 (`pcall-begin/arg/enter` with `new`) | P2 |\n322:| yang.php: member calls go through one `php/method-call` seam (`getMessage`, `getCode`, `getPrevious` on Throwable; `bindTo`, `__invoke` on Closure); `bindTo` shares statics with the source closure (PHP copies them); `new` and classes are refused; the call protocol validates a named argument's name at entry, so in `f(1, z: 2, w: side())` `side()` runs where PHP stops at `z` (C28, `G-method-seam`); fixture `:call-unknown-named-later-arg-runs` (oracle-only, pending) | Stage 0 gate D5 and section 3; `e2e-test/gate-fix-programs-test` | yang.php | P4 S2 (class model) and P4 S4 (`pcall-begin/arg/enter` with `new`) | P2 |\n332:| yang.clojure: defmacro parameters are the one binder surface skipping check-binder!/reserved-prefix validation (consciously deferred: the (defmacro defn [& xs]) test needs &); a reserved-prefix macro param can be shadowed by a generated cursor; macros never enter the convention so impact is body-level only; architect disposition: ledger row, closing route = &-aware per-param binder check, slice 4 with the nested-def refusal | slice 3b review (glm session 79d4df98) | yang.clojure | slice 4 | P3 |\n335:| yang.clojure: three slice-4 residuals, bundled per architect disposition (fable 1793212600000): (1) a free REFERENCE to a reserved-prefix worker name (dsg__loop0 etc.) is not refused — binder enforcement covers bindings only, so user-typed (dsg__loop0 dsg__loop0 3) inside a 2-binding loop reaches the worker and nil-fills; closing route: a compile-program pre-pass refusing reserved-prefix symbols in any position; (2) bare recur/loop symbols in VALUE position compile as ordinary variables (host Clojure rejects unbound recur; binder-shadowed case matches Clojure); closing route: same pre-pass refusing recur/loop outside operator position; (3) the wrong-operand-count rejection message says \"loop bindings\" also for function-level targets (cosmetic; target records its kind) | slice 4 review (glm session 5ff7ec63, verified against compile-loop/clojure.cljc:879-955 and ast_walker.cljc zero :tail? references) | yang.clojure | slice 5 (all three: one pre-pass rides the outcome-channel work) | P3 |\n340:| yang.clojure: the and/or if-chain expansions bind host gensym names (and__/or__) outside the dsg__ reserved-prefix regime that slice 5 hardens; a colliding user-typed and__<n> would shadow inside the expansion; closing route: reserved-pref