{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '300,390p;2425,2695p;2745,2810p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | sed -n '370,460p'\"","aggregated_output":"   300\t(defn- seal-of\n   301\t  \"The seal of a `kind` reference to resource `id` under `secret`.\"\n   302\t  [secret kind id]\n   303\t  (jing/content-hash [:yin.k/seal secret kind id] {:algorithm :blake3}))\n   304\t\n   305\t\n   306\t(defn- cursor-cell?\n   307\t  \"True when a resource is a cursor cell, `{:stream-id id :cursor c}`.\n   308\t   A cursor cell is the VM's mutable box (with identity) holding one\n   309\t   immutable `dao.stream` cursor; `:stream/next` overwrites its `:cursor`\n   310\t   with the successor. A guest program holds a sealed `:cursor-ref` naming\n   311\t   it, never the cell itself. Not to be confused with `yin.vm.cell`, the\n   312\t   general heap box. Vocabulary: UCF §7.5.3, \\\"Terminology\\\".\"\n   313\t  [resource]\n   314\t  (and (map? resource) (contains? resource :stream-id)))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\t(defn issue-ref\n   318\t  \"A reference of `kind` (`:stream-ref`, `:cursor-ref`, or `:cell-ref`) to\n   319\t   resource or heap cell `id`, sealed under the task's capability secret.\n   320\t   A task composed\n   321\t   without a secret cannot issue one: it fails closed rather than issue a\n   322\t   reference anyone could forge.\"\n   323\t  [state kind id]\n   324\t  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)]\n   325\t    (when (nil? secret)\n   326\t      (fail (str \"This task has no capability secret, so it cannot issue\"\n   327\t                 \" a resource reference\")\n   328\t            {:reason :no-capability-secret, :kind kind, :id id}))\n   329\t    {:type kind, :id id, :seal (seal-of secret kind id)}))\n   330\t\n   331\t\n   332\t(defn authentic-ref?\n   333\t  \"True when `ref` is a `kind` reference this task issued: its seal\n   334\t   verifies under the task's secret, and it names a live resource of that\n   335\t   kind. A `:cell-ref` is checked against `:heap` instead: its id is live\n   336\t   by `contains?` (a cell may hold nil) and its seal equals the one the\n   337\t   heap entry recorded at allocation, so no hash is computed per access.\"\n   338\t  [state kind ref]\n   339\t  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)\n   340\t        id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))]\n   341\t    (if (= :cell-ref kind)\n   342\t      (let [heap (:heap state)]\n   343\t        (boolean (and (some? secret)\n   344\t                      (= kind (:type ref))\n   345\t                      (contains? heap id)\n   346\t                      (= (:seal ref) (:seal (get heap id))))))\n   347\t      (let [resource (get (:resources state) id)]\n   348\t        (boolean (and (some? secret)\n   349\t                      (= kind (:type ref))\n   350\t                      (some? resource)\n   351\t                      (= (:seal ref) (seal-of secret kind id))\n   352\t                      (= (= :cursor-ref kind) (cursor-cell? resource))))))))\n   353\t\n   354\t\n   355\t(defn check-ref!\n   356\t  \"The resource id a program-supplied `kind` reference names, once its\n   357\t   seal verifies (r10). Anything else fails closed with\n   358\t   `:forged-resource-reference`, naming the effect and the id it named;\n   359\t   a cell ref whose id the heap does not hold is\n   360\t   `:dead-or-forged-reference` instead: its cell was swept, or never was.\n   361\t   Ids are never reused, so such a ref is never silently reallocated.\"\n   362\t  [state effect-kind kind ref]\n   363\t  (if (authentic-ref? state kind ref)\n   364\t    (:id ref)\n   365\t    (let [id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))\n   366\t          dead? (and (= :cell-ref kind) (not (contains? (:heap state) id)))]\n   367\t      (fail (if dead? \"Dead or forged cell reference\" \"Forged resource reference\")\n   368\t            {:reason (if dead?\n   369\t                       :dead-or-forged-reference\n   370\t                       :forged-resource-reference),\n   371\t             :effect effect-kind,\n   372\t             :kind kind,\n   373\t             :id id}))))\n   374\t\n   375\t\n   376\t(declare gensym)\n   377\t\n   378\t\n   379\t(defn attach-resource\n   380\t  \"Install the host stream `handle` a composition hands a task under a\n   381\t   fresh resource id, and return `[stream-ref state]` with the reference\n   382\t   sealed under the task's secret. This is how a stream reaches a program:\n   383\t   never through the store.\"\n   384\t  [state handle]\n   385\t  (let [[id state] (gensym state \"stream\")\n   386\t        ref (issue-ref state :stream-ref id)]\n   387\t    [ref (assoc-in state [:resources id] handle)]))\n   388\t\n   389\t\n   390\t(def ^:private wake-error-outcomes\n  2425\t   effect result and costs nothing on an ordinary call. A callable with\n  2426\t   no profile is the composition's trusted value and passes. Returns\n  2427\t   `state`, carrying the index it checked against, for the caller to\n  2428\t   dispatch the effect on.\"\n  2429\t  [state f effect]\n  2430\t  (let [state (with-primitive-effects state)\n  2431\t        from-primitives (get (:index (:callable-effects state)) f)\n  2432\t        from-modules (get (:callable-effects (:modules state)) f)\n  2433\t        declared (if (and from-primitives from-modules)\n  2434\t                   (into from-primitives from-modules)\n  2435\t                   (or from-primitives from-modules))]\n  2436\t    (if (and declared (not (contains? declared (:effect effect))))\n  2437\t      (fail \"Effect outside the callee's declared profile\"\n  2438\t            {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undeclared-effect,\n  2439\t             :yin.k/effect (:effect effect),\n  2440\t             :yin.k/effects declared})\n  2441\t      state)))\n  2442\t\n  2443\t\n  2444\t(defn- heap-write\n  2445\t  \"`state` with heap cell `id` holding `v` under `seal`: allocation when the\n  2446\t   cell is new, a write (the seal unchanged) when it is live.\"\n  2447\t  [state id seal v]\n  2448\t  (assoc-in state [:heap id] {:value v, :seal seal}))\n  2449\t\n  2450\t\n  2451\t;; =============================================================================\n  2452\t;; Heap reclamation (Architect heap-reclamation design, slice 1)\n  2453\t;; =============================================================================\n  2454\t;;\n  2455\t;; A deterministic, allocation-triggered, stop-the-world mark-sweep over\n  2456\t;; `:heap`, as a pure `vm -> vm'`. The `:cell/new` arm counts allocations in\n  2457\t;; `:gc` and collects when the count reaches the threshold, so two runs\n  2458\t;; collect at the same allocation. Marking runs over the heap as it was when\n  2459\t;; the cycle began (a persistent map, so the snapshot is a reference) and the\n  2460\t;; sweep removes only ids of that snapshot: an id allocated at or after the\n  2461\t;; cycle's counter start is not in it and is spared. A budgeted marker can\n  2462\t;; later run the same `trace` k steps per round. Ids are never reused:\n  2463\t;; `:id-counter` only grows, so a ref to a swept cell names nothing and is\n  2464\t;; refused `:dead-or-forged-reference`.\n  2465\t\n  2466\t(defn- heap-ref-id\n  2467\t  \"The id the map `x` names when it is a `:cell-ref` authentic against\n  2468\t   `heap`, else nil.\"\n  2469\t  [heap x]\n  2470\t  (when (= :cell-ref (:type x))\n  2471\t    (let [id (:id x)\n  2472\t          entry (get heap id)]\n  2473\t      (when (and (some? entry) (= (:seal x) (:seal entry))) id))))\n  2474\t\n  2475\t\n  2476\t(defn- moded\n  2477\t  \"`work` with each of `xs` pushed in `mode`, `:kernel` or `:data`.\"\n  2478\t  [work mode xs]\n  2479\t  (into work (map (fn [x] [mode x])) xs))\n  2480\t\n  2481\t\n  2482\t(defn- identity-hash\n  2483\t  \"The host's identity hash of `o`: one number per object, whatever the\n  2484\t   object's size. It reads no field of `o`, so a continuation holding a\n  2485\t   thousand-frame chain costs what a scalar costs.\"\n  2486\t  [o]\n  2487\t  #?(:clj (System/identityHashCode o)\n  2488\t     :cljs (goog/getUid o)\n  2489\t     :cljd (dart-core/identityHashCode o)))\n  2490\t\n  2491\t\n  2492\t;; `trace` cannot key its seen set on `(hash [mode value])`, the shape a\n  2493\t;; Clojure set asks for: a closure's and a continuation's `-hash` is\n  2494\t;; structural over kind, owner and payload by law (`yin.vm.values`, table C),\n  2495\t;; so hashing one recurses through its whole payload — the captured\n  2496\t;; environments, the continuation chain below, the AST bodies those hold. A\n  2497\t;; guest that has grown a 1000-frame handler chain then exhausts the host\n  2498\t;; stack inside the collector, long before its own recursion guard fires\n  2499\t;; (stack audit r2: a 13,542-frame trace, every frame a `hash`).\n  2500\t;;\n  2501\t;; Identity is also the sounder key, and not only the cheaper one. Nothing\n  2502\t;; is missed by it: a value already walked is the same object, and an\n  2503\t;; equal-but-distinct one is walked again, finding the same ids. `found` —\n  2504\t;; hence the heap the sweep leaves — is what value-keyed dedup computed.\n  2505\t(deftype Visited\n  2506\t  [mode o]\n  2507\t  #?@(:cljd [cljd.core/IEquiv\n  2508\t             (-equiv [_ other]\n  2509\t                     (and (instance? Visited other)\n  2510\t                          (= mode (.-mode ^Visited other))\n  2511\t                          (identical? o (.-o ^Visited other))))\n  2512\t             cljd.core/IHash\n  2513\t             (-hash [_] (bit-xor (hash mode) (identity-hash o)))]\n  2514\t      :clj [Object\n  2515\t            (equals [_ other]\n  2516\t                    (and (instance? Visited other)\n  2517\t                         (= mode (.-mode ^Visited other))\n  2518\t                         (identical? o (.-o ^Visited other))))\n  2519\t            (hashCode [_] (bit-xor (hash mode) (identity-hash o)))\n  2520\t            clojure.lang.IHashEq\n  2521\t            (hasheq [_] (bit-xor (hash mode) (identity-hash o)))]\n  2522\t      :cljs [IEquiv\n  2523\t             (-equiv [_ other]\n  2524\t                     (and (instance? Visited other)\n  2525\t                          (= mode (.-mode ^Visited other))\n  2526\t                          (identical? o (.-o ^Visited other))))\n  2527\t             IHash\n  2528\t             (-hash [_] (bit-xor (hash mode) (identity-hash o)))]))\n  2529\t\n  2530\t\n  2531\t(defn- trace\n  2532\t  \"`found` plus the ids of `heap` reachable from `roots`, a map\n  2533\t   `{:kernel [...] :data [...]}` of root values by mode. Two modes keep\n  2534\t   guest data from being read as kernel shapes (gemini reclamation gate,\n  2535\t   concern 1):\n  2536\t\n  2537\t   - `:kernel`, a value in a kernel position (a kernel root, an engine\n  2538\t     table entry, a closure or continuation payload, or a kernel child of\n  2539\t     one): the kernel's `gc-children` may interpret it, and answers which\n  2540\t     of its children are kernel positions and which are values. A value\n  2541\t     it does not recognize is walked whole, as data.\n  2542\t   - `:data`, a value position (an environment value, an operand, a\n  2543\t     register, a cell's content): every map is walked whole, never\n  2544\t     pruned, so a guest map shaped like a frame cannot hide a cell ref.\n  2545\t     Only a closure or continuation, a host type no guest can forge,\n  2546\t     re-enters `:kernel` mode through its payload.\n  2547\t\n  2548\t   Scalars hold nothing. With `follow?` a newly found id's content is\n  2549\t   traced too, as data (marking); without, only the refs met directly\n  2550\t   (pinning). Each object is visited once per mode, so shared environments\n  2551\t   cost one walk and a cell holding its own ref terminates; the visit is\n  2552\t   keyed on identity (`Visited`), never on a value's structural hash,\n  2553\t   which for a closure or a continuation would recurse through the whole\n  2554\t   chain it holds. The worklist is explicit: a deep continuation chain\n  2555\t   does not grow the host stack.\"\n  2556\t  [vm heap roots found follow?]\n  2557\t  (let [children-of (if (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\n  2558\t                      #(module/gc-children vm %)\n  2559\t                      (constantly nil))]\n  2560\t    (loop [work (-> ()\n  2561\t                    (moded :kernel (:kernel roots))\n  2562\t                    (moded :data (:data roots)))\n  2563\t           seen #{}\n  2564\t           found found]\n  2565\t      (if (empty? work)\n  2566\t        found\n  2567\t        (let [[mode x] (peek work)\n  2568\t              work (pop work)\n  2569\t              visit (when-not (scalar? x) (Visited. mode x))]\n  2570\t          (if (or (nil? visit) (contains? seen visit))\n  2571\t            (recur work seen found)\n  2572\t            (let [id (when (map? x) (heap-ref-id heap x))\n  2573\t                  new-id? (and (some? id) (not (contains? found id)))\n  2574\t                  children (when (and (= :kernel mode)\n  2575\t                                      (not (values/host-typed? x)))\n  2576\t                             (children-of x))\n  2577\t                  work (cond-> work\n  2578\t                         (and new-id? follow?)\n  2579\t                         (conj [:data (:value (get heap id))])\n  2580\t                         (values/host-typed? x)\n  2581\t                         (conj [:kernel (values/payload x)])\n  2582\t                         (some? children)\n  2583\t                         (-> (moded :kernel (:kernel children))\n  2584\t                             (moded :data (:values children)))\n  2585\t                         (and (nil? children) (map? x))\n  2586\t                         (-> (moded :data (keys x))\n  2587\t                             (moded :data (vals x)))\n  2588\t                         (and (nil? children) (not (map? x)) (coll? x))\n  2589\t                         (moded :data x))]\n  2590\t              (recur work\n  2591\t                     (conj seen visit)\n  2592\t                     (if new-id? (conj found id) found)))))))))\n  2593\t\n  2594\t\n  2595\t(defn- gc-roots\n  2596\t  \"Every root of `vm` (design Q1), by mode: the kernel's registers as it\n  2597\t   classifies them (`module/gc-roots`), each entry of `:parked`,\n  2598\t   `:wait-set` and `:ready-queue` as a kernel position, the store and\n  2599\t   every module store as values, then `extra` as values. Code, images,\n  2600\t   the registry, primitives, `:callable-effects`, telemetry and\n  2601\t   `:resources` are not roots: a literal can never be an authentic ref,\n  2602\t   and a value inside a stream is the medium's (hence pinning).\"\n  2603\t  [vm extra]\n  2604\t  (let [kernel (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\n  2605\t                 (module/gc-roots vm))]\n  2606\t    {:kernel (-> (vec (:kernel kernel))\n  2607\t                 (into (vals (:parked vm)))\n  2608\t                 (into (:wait-set vm))\n  2609\t                 (into (:ready-queue vm))),\n  2610\t     :data (-> [(:store vm) (:module-stores vm)]\n  2611\t               (into (:values kernel))\n  2612\t               (into extra))}))\n  2613\t\n  2614\t\n  2615\t(defn- mark\n  2616\t  \"The ids of `heap` live from `roots` and from the `pinned` ids: a pinned\n  2617\t   cell is a root, so its content is traced too, as data.\"\n  2618\t  [vm heap roots pinned]\n  2619\t  (let [pins (filterv #(contains? heap %) pinned)]\n  2620\t    (trace vm\n  2621\t           heap\n  2622\t           (update roots :data into (map #(:value (get heap %))) pins)\n  2623\t           (set pins)\n  2624\t           true)))\n  2625\t\n  2626\t\n  2627\t(defn- sweep\n  2628\t  \"`heap` without each id of the cycle's `snapshot` that `marked` lacks.\n  2629\t   An id allocated after the snapshot is not in it, so it is spared.\"\n  2630\t  [heap snapshot marked]\n  2631\t  (reduce-kv (fn [h id _] (if (contains? marked id) h (dissoc h id)))\n  2632\t             heap\n  2633\t             snapshot))\n  2634\t\n  2635\t\n  2636\t(defn- gc-of\n  2637\t  [state]\n  2638\t  (or (:gc state) (vm/fresh-gc nil)))\n  2639\t\n  2640\t\n  2641\t(defn collect\n  2642\t  \"`vm` after one stop-the-world collection of its `:heap`, with `extra`\n  2643\t   traced as additional roots. The allocation count restarts and the\n  2644\t   threshold becomes `max(base, 2 x live)`, so the total work stays linear\n  2645\t   in allocations. Pure: the same state always collects to the same heap.\"\n  2646\t  ([vm] (collect vm nil))\n  2647\t  ([vm extra]\n  2648\t   (let [gc (gc-of vm)\n  2649\t         snapshot (:heap vm)\n  2650\t         marked (mark vm snapshot (gc-roots vm extra) (:pinned gc))\n  2651\t         heap (sweep (:heap vm) snapshot marked)]\n  2652\t     (assoc vm\n  2653\t            :heap heap\n  2654\t            :gc (assoc gc\n  2655\t                       :since 0\n  2656\t                       :threshold (max (:base gc) (* 2 (count heap))))))))\n  2657\t\n  2658\t\n  2659\t(defn- count-allocation\n  2660\t  \"`state` with one allocation counted, collected first when the count\n  2661\t   reaches the threshold. `v`, the value being boxed, is held by no\n  2662\t   register yet, so it is traced as an extra root.\"\n  2663\t  [state v]\n  2664\t  (let [gc (gc-of state)\n  2665\t        since (inc (:since gc))]\n  2666\t    (if (>= since (:threshold gc))\n  2667\t      (collect state [v])\n  2668\t      (assoc state :gc (assoc gc :since since)))))\n  2669\t\n  2670\t\n  2671\t(defn pin-refs\n  2672\t  \"`state` with every cell `v` holds a ref to pinned for the task's life\n  2673\t   (owner decision 1). A value appended to a stream or carried by an FFI\n  2674\t   request leaves the VM's view, so no trace could find a ref inside it\n  2675\t   when it comes back.\"\n  2676\t  [state v]\n  2677\t  (if (or (scalar? v) (empty? (:heap state)))\n  2678\t    state\n  2679\t    (let [ids (trace state (:heap state) {:data [v]} #{} false)]\n  2680\t      (if (seq ids)\n  2681\t        (assoc state :gc (update (gc-of state) :pinned into ids))\n  2682\t        state))))\n  2683\t\n  2684\t\n  2685\t(defn handle-effect\n  2686\t  \"Dispatch an effect and return {:state updated-state :value v :blocked? bool}.\n  2687\t   park-entry-fns maps :stream/put and :stream/next to functions that build\n  2688\t   wait entries.\n  2689\t\n  2690\t   `effect` must be a `yin.vm.effect` value minted by `module/make-effect`\n  2691\t   (D4); a map, whatever its keys, is data and is refused here.\n  2692\t\n  2693\t   A parked entry is stored as the builder left it plus, for a writer, the\n  2694\t   `:datom` it retries: registers and resource ids only. Neither the live\n  2695\t   stream handle nor a restore closure is attached — `check-wait-set`\n  2745\t                                  (park-entry state effect result))]\n  2746\t                (handle-stream-block result built-entry))\n  2747\t              {:state (:state result),\n  2748\t               :value (:value result),\n  2749\t               :blocked? false}))\n  2750\t          :stream/poll\n  2751\t          (let [result (handle-poll state effect)]\n  2752\t            (if (and (:park result) (= :running (vm/gate-mode state)))\n  2753\t              (let [builder (or (get park-entry-fns :stream/poll)\n  2754\t                                (get park-entry-fns :stream/next))\n  2755\t                    built (when builder (builder state effect result))]\n  2756\t                (handle-stream-block\n  2757\t                  result\n  2758\t                  (when built\n  2759\t                    (assoc built\n  2760\t                           :reason :observe\n  2761\t                           :op :poll\n  2762\t                           :cursor-ref (:cursor-ref result)\n  2763\t                           :stream-id (:stream-id result)))))\n  2764\t              {:state (:state result),\n  2765\t               :value (:value result),\n  2766\t               :blocked? false}))\n  2767\t          :stream/close\n  2768\t          (let [_ (gate-refuse! state effect)\n  2769\t                close-result (handle-close state effect)]\n  2770\t            {:state (:state close-result), :value nil, :blocked? false})\n  2771\t          ;; `:heap` is VM state, not continuation state: a write is seen\n  2772\t          ;; by every holder of the ref and survives continuation invocation\n  2773\t          :cell/new\n  2774\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym (count-allocation state (:val effect)) \"cell\")\n  2775\t                ref (issue-ref s' :cell-ref id)]\n  2776\t            {:state (heap-write s' id (:seal ref) (:val effect)),\n  2777\t             :value ref,\n  2778\t             :blocked? false})\n  2779\t          :cell/get\n  2780\t          (let [id (check-ref! state :cell/get :cell-ref (:cell effect))]\n  2781\t            ;; the content is answered as data, never re-interpreted\n  2782\t            {:state state,\n  2783\t             :value (get-in state [:heap id :value]),\n  2784\t             :blocked? false})\n  2785\t          :cell/set!\n  2786\t          (let [id (check-ref! state :cell/set! :cell-ref (:cell effect))]\n  2787\t            {:state (heap-write state id (get-in state [:heap id :seal])\n  2788\t                                (:val effect)),\n  2789\t             :value (:val effect),\n  2790\t             :blocked? false})\n  2791\t          ;; The cell-ref ruling of record: the same heap+seal predicate\n  2792\t          ;; `check-ref!` consults (r10), answered as data instead of\n  2793\t          ;; failing closed, so compiled call routing can ask the issuer\n  2794\t          ;; whether it issued a reference. A pure query: no state change,\n  2795\t          ;; never fatal, and the engine learns no frontend semantics.\n  2796\t          :cell/authentic?\n  2797\t          {:state state,\n  2798\t           :value (authentic-ref? state :cell-ref (:cell effect)),\n  2799\t           :blocked? false}\n  2800\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"effect\")\n  2801\t                handler (module/get-effect-handler (:modules state)\n  2802\t                                                   (:effect effect))]\n  2803\t            (if handler\n  2804\t              (handler s' effect (assoc opts :id id))\n  2805\t              (fail \"Unknown effect\" {:effect (:effect effect)}))))]\n  2806\t    (update result\n  2807\t            :state\n  2808\t            (fn [result-state]\n  2809\t              (telemetry/emit-snapshot (assoc result-state\n  2810\t                                              :value (:value result))\n   370\t  [registry]\n   371\t  (register-host-module registry 'stream stream-module stream-profiles))\n   372\t\n   373\t\n   374\t;; =============================================================================\n   375\t;; The `cell` module\n   376\t;; =============================================================================\n   377\t;;\n   378\t;; A cell is a mutable location in the task's `:heap`, reached by a sealed\n   379\t;; `:cell-ref` (Architect cell ruling, slice 1). These are pure effect\n   380\t;; constructors like the stream module's: they touch no heap, and the engine\n   381\t;; interprets the effects they return. The heap is VM state, so a mutation\n   382\t;; is shared by every closure over the ref and is never rolled back when a\n   383\t;; continuation is invoked (box semantics). Beside the three mutators the\n   384\t;; module publishes `authentic?`, the ruling-of-record query a caller's\n   385\t;; compiled code asks the issuer before dereferencing a cell-ref-shaped\n   386\t;; callee; it answers a boolean and changes nothing.\n   387\t\n   388\t(defn new-cell\n   389\t  [v]\n   390\t  (make-effect :cell/new {:val v}))\n   391\t\n   392\t\n   393\t(defn get-cell\n   394\t  [c]\n   395\t  (make-effect :cell/get {:cell c}))\n   396\t\n   397\t\n   398\t(defn set-cell!\n   399\t  [c v]\n   400\t  (make-effect :cell/set! {:cell c, :val v}))\n   401\t\n   402\t\n   403\t(defn authentic-cell?\n   404\t  \"The pure query the cell-ref ruling of record added: does the heap\n   405\t   issue `c` as a cell reference? The engine answers the same\n   406\t   heap+seal predicate `check-ref!` consults, as a boolean, so compiled\n   407\t   call routing can ask the issuer instead of guessing from a value's\n   408\t   shape. Non-fatal, state unchanged.\"\n   409\t  [c]\n   410\t  (make-effect :cell/authentic? {:cell c}))\n   411\t\n   412\t\n   413\t(def cell-module\n   414\t  \"The `cell` module definition. Registering it is a composition step.\"\n   415\t  {'new new-cell, 'get get-cell, 'set! set-cell!, 'authentic? authentic-cell?})\n   416\t\n   417\t\n   418\t(def cell-profiles\n   419\t  \"UCF 7.5.2 profiles for the `cell` module's bindings: each an\n   420\t   `:effectful` pure effect constructor declaring its one effect kind.\"\n   421\t  {'new (vm/primitive-profile 'new :effectful [1] #{:cell/new} :none)\n   422\t   'get (vm/primitive-profile 'get :effectful [1] #{:cell/get} :none)\n   423\t   'set! (vm/primitive-profile 'set! :effectful [2] #{:cell/set!} :none)\n   424\t   'authentic? (vm/primitive-profile 'authentic? :effectful [1]\n   425\t                                     #{:cell/authentic?} :none)})\n   426\t\n   427\t\n   428\t(defn register-cell-module\n   429\t  \"Return registry with the `cell` module registered.\"\n   430\t  [registry]\n   431\t  (register-host-module registry 'cell cell-module cell-profiles))\n   432\t\n   433\t\n   434\t;; =============================================================================\n   435\t;; Built-in effect handlers\n   436\t;; =============================================================================\n   437\t\n   438\t;; =============================================================================\n   439\t;; `require` lowers to the linker (yin.vm.linker.md section 7)\n   440\t;; =============================================================================\n   441\t\n   442\t(defprotocol IModuleKernel\n   443\t  \"What a kernel supplies the install child and the `linked` transition\n   444\t   (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3). Every method is a pure function of a\n   445\t   VM value; the engine owns the phases, the kernel owns its coordinates.\"\n   446\t\n   447\t  (link-format\n   448\t    [vm]\n   449\t    \"`{:format kw :contract s}`: the format this kernel links, and the\n   450\t     execution contract it runs.\")\n   451\t\n   452\t  (spawn-module\n   453\t    [vm image opts]\n   454\t    \"A fresh VM of this backend with the verified `image` loaded by the\n   455\t     ordinary loader, holding nothing of `vm`'s state but its composition\n   456\t     values (primitives, stream constructor, link pair). `opts` carries\n   457\t     `:modules` (the child's module view), `:origin`, and `:ancestry`.\")\n   458\t\n   459\t  (image-identity\n   460\t    [vm image]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
