 a top-level defn preserves dynamic admission and routing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n     (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\\\\\\\\n-      (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\\\\\\\\n-                            :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee 5}}]\\\\\\\\n+      (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\\\\\\\\n+                            :yang.call/value {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\\\\\\\\n+                                              :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee 5}}}]\\\\\\\\n              (run-library '[(defn f\\\\\\\\n                               [x]\\\\\\\\n                               (+ x 100))\\\\\\\\n@@ -2653,8 +2766,9 @@\\\\\\\\n         (is (= :yin.k/error tag))\\\\\\\\n         (is (= :yang.call/not-callable (:yang.call/reason payload))\\\\\\\\n             \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"entry-present forged local map routes to admission and refuses\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\n-      (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\\\\\\\\n-                            :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee 5}}]\\\\\\\\n+      (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\\\\\\\\n+                            :yang.call/value {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable\\\\\\\\n+                                              :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee 5}}}]\\\\\\\\n              (run-library '[(defn f\\\\\\\\n                               [[f]]\\\\\\\\n                               (f 1))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff -w 8cd9fc92..778747ce -- src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_7\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cat .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md; sed -n '1,190p' .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py; rg --files collab/exception-track | rg '1794320926000|1794332020000|1794336505000'; git rev-parse HEAD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_7\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cat .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md; sed -n '1,190p' .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py; rg --files collab/exception-track | rg '1794320926000|1794332020000|1794336505000'; git rev-parse HEAD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"# Code Review PR Checklist & Taxonomy\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nWhen performing code reviews, evaluate changes using this structured checklist and severity taxonomy.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. Finding Severity Taxonomy\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Severity | Label | Definition | Examples |\\\\\\\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\\\\\\\n| **P0** | **Critical (Blocker)** | Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, production crashes, secret leakage. Must be fixed before merging. | Hardcoded tokens, unhandled NullPointer on critical path, SQL injection, broken auth check. |\\\\\\\\n| **P1** | **High (Must Address)** | Logic bugs, breaking API changes, missing error handling on external calls, race conditions, lack of tests for complex logic. | Swallowed exceptions, broken retry loop, missing backward compatibility in API schema. |\\\\\\\\n| **P2** | **Medium (Recommended)** | Performance inefficiencies, code duplication, sub-optimal data structures, non-idiomatic style. | Unnecessary DB query inside loop, missing index, missing parameter validation. |\\\\\\\\n| **P3** | **Low (Nit / Suggestion)** | Minor formatting, naming improvements, leftover comments/TODOs, minor doc polish. | Variable naming clarity, typos in docstrings, cleaning leftover TODO comments. |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. Comprehensive Review Checklist\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### A. Logic & Correctness\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Does the code handle null/nil/undefined, empty collections, zero values, boundary numbers, and unexpected inputs?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **State & Concurrency**: Are shared state mutations thread-safe? Are locks acquired/released properly without deadlock risks?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Control Flow**: Are all conditional branches covered? Do loops have guaranteed termination conditions?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Error Propagation**: Are errors caught and logged/surfaced appropriately, rather than swallowed silently (`catch (Exception e) {}`)?\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### B. Security & Credentials\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **No Hardcoded Secrets**: Are API keys, passwords, bearer tokens, or private keys excluded from code and config?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Input Validation & Sanitization**: Are external inputs validated before processing or passing to system shells, DB queries, or HTML rendering?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Authentication & Authorization**: Do endpoints verify user identity and check permissions before executing state changes?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Safe Dependencies**: Are newly added packages pinned to trusted versions without known vulnerabilities?\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### C. Architecture & API Design\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Preserve API Contracts**: Are public method signatures, REST endpoints, and schema definitions backward compatible?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Single Responsibility**: Are modules, classes, and functions focused on a clear, single responsibility?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Coupling & Cohesion**: Is the new code properly modularized without introducing circular dependencies or leaky abstractions?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Idempotence**: Are retry loops or state-changing operations safe to re-execute on transient failures?\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### D. Performance & Resource Efficiency\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **N+1 Queries**: Are database or remote API calls executed in batches rather than inside loops?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Resource Cleanup**: Are file handles, database connections, streams, and web sockets closed explicitly (or managed via try-with-resources / context managers)?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Memory & Allocation**: Are large datasets streamed or paginated rather than loaded fully into memory at once?\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### E. Test Coverage & Quality\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Test Coverage**: Do new features or bug fixes include corresponding unit or integration tests?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Test Quality**: Do tests verify actual assertions rather than just checking that code runs without throwing?\\\\\\\\n- [ ] **Edge Case Tests**: Are failure modes, invalid inputs, and error handlers covered by unit tests?\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 3. Review Feedback Guidelines\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Be Specific**: Always reference the exact file line number, function name, and context.\\\\\\\\n2. **Explain the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Why\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"**: Don't just say \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"change this\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". Explain the risk or benefit (e.g., \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"This could lead to a race condition if two threads call `transact!` simultaneously...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").\\\\\\\\n3. **Provide Concrete Fixes**: Offer concrete, copy-pasteable diff snippets where appropriate.\\\\\\\\n4. **Acknowledge Good Work**: Highlight well-crafted solutions, thorough tests, or clean refactorings.\\\\\\\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nPR Reviewer Utility Script for Git-based Code Reviews.\\\\\\\\nParses git diffs, analyzes churn and file risk categories, scans for security smells\\\\\\\\nand debugging code, and produces structured markdown or JSON review reports.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nimport argparse\\\\\\\\nimport json\\\\\\\\nimport os\\\\\\\\nimport re\\\\\\\\nimport subprocess\\\\\\\\nimport sys\\\\\\\\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\\\\\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\\\\\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n@dataclass\\\\\\\\nclass Finding:\\\\\\\\n    severity: str  # P0 (Critical), P1 (High), P2 (Medium), P3 (Low)\\\\\\\\n    category: str  # Security, Debug, Quality, ErrorHandling, TestCoverage\\\\\\\\n    file_path: str\\\\\\\\n    line_number: Optional[int]\\\\\\\\n    message: str\\\\\\\\n    snippet: str\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n@dataclass\\\\\\\\nclass FileStat:\\\\\\\\n    path: str\\\\\\\\n    additions: int\\\\\\\\n    deletions: int\\\\\\\\n    category: str\\\\\\\\n    risk_level: str  # High, Medium, Low\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n@dataclass\\\\\\\\nclass ReviewSummary:\\\\\\\\n    target: str\\\\\\\\n    total_files: int\\\\\\\\n    total_additions: int\\\\\\\\n    total_deletions: int\\\\\\\\n    test_additions: int\\\\\\\\n    source_additions: int\\\\\\\\n    test_to_source_ratio: float\\\\\\\\n    file_stats: List[FileStat] = field(default_factory=list)\\\\\\\\n    findings: List[Finding] = field(default_factory=list)\\\\\\\\n    commits: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef run_git_command(args: List[str], cwd: Optional[str] = None) -> str:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Helper to run git commands cleanly.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    cmd = [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"git\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"] + args\\\\\\\\n    try:\\\\\\\\n        res = subprocess.run(\\\\\\\\n            cmd,\\\\\\\\n            cwd=cwd,\\\\\\\\n            stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\\\\\\\\n            stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\\\\\\\\n            text=True,\\\\\\\\n            check=True,\\\\\\\\n        )\\\\\\\\n        return res.stdout.strip()\\\\\\\\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\\\\\\\\n        sys.stderr.write(f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Git command failed: {' '.join(cmd)}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nError: {e.stderr}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Git execution failed: {e.stderr.strip()}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef categorize_file(file_path: str) -> Tuple[str, str]:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Categorizes file type and assigns risk level.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    path_lower = file_path.lower()\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Security & Auth\\\\\\\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"auth\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"secret\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"crypto\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"token\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"permission\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"jwt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"oauth\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"password\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]):\\\\\\\\n        return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Security/Auth\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"High\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Database & Schema\\\\\\\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"migration\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".sql\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"entity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"db/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]):\\\\\\\\n        return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Database/Schema\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"High\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Infrastructure & Config\\\\\\\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"docker\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"terraform\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".tf\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".env\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"k8s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"helm\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ci/cd\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".github/workflows\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]):\\\\\\\\n        return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Infra/Config\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"High\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    if any(file_path.endswith(ext) for ext in [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"package.json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"deps.edn\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Cargo.toml\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"go.mod\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"requirements.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"pom.xml\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"build.gradle\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]):\\\\\\\\n        return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Medium\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # API / Interfaces\\\\\\\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"proto\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"openapi\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"swagger\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"graphql\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"router\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"controller\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"api/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]):\\\\\\\\n        return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"API/Contract\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Medium\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Tests\\\\\\\\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"spec\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"mock\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fixture\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"e2e\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]):\\\\\\\\n        return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Tests\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Low\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Documentation\\\\\\\\n    if any(file_path.endswith(ext) for ext in [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".rst\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"LICENSE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]):\\\\\\\\n        return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Documentation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Low\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Core source\\\\\\\\n    return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Source Code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Medium\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef scan_diff_content(diff_text: str) -> List[Finding]:\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Scans diff text for added code smells and risks.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    findings: List[Finding] = []\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    # Patterns to match added lines\\\\\\\\n    patterns = [\\\\\\\\n        # Secret leaks\\\\\\\\n        (\\\\\\\\n            r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?i)^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\+.*(api[_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\-]?key|secret[_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\-]?key|bearer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s+[a-z0-9_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.]{20,}|private[_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\-]?key)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[:=]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"][A-Za-z0-9%+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\/=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\-_]{8,}['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Security\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Possible hardcoded credential or secret detected.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        ),\\\\\\\\n        (\\\\\\\\n            r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\+.*-----BEGIN (RSA|OPENSSH|EC|PRIVATE) KEY-----\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Security\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Embedded private key detected.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        ),\\\\\\\\n        # Debug code left behind\\\\\\\\n        (\\\\\\\\n            r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\+.*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(console\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.log|print\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\(|debugger;|binding\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.pry|import pdb; pdb\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.set_trace|println!|fmt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.Println)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Debug\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Leftover debug statement detected.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        ),\\\\\\\\n        # Dangerous functions\\\\\\\\n        (\\\\\\\\n            r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\+.*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(eval\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\(|exec\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\(|os\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.system\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\(|subprocess\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.Popen\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\(.*shell\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*True|dangerouslySetInnerHTML)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Security\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Potentially unsafe dynamic execution or shell invocation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        ),\\\\\\\\n        # Swallowed exceptions\\\\\\\\n        (\\\\\\\\n            r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\+.*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(catch\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\([^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\)]*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\}|except:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*pass|rescue\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*=>\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*nil)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ErrorHandling\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Swallowed exception without logging or handling.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        ),\\\\\\\\n        # Potential SQL Injection\\\\\\\\n        (\\\\\\\\n            r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?i)^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\+.*((select|insert|update|delete)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s+.*%s|(select|insert|update|delete)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s+.*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\$[a-z0-9_]+|(select|insert|update|delete)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s+.*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[a-z0-9_]+)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"P1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Security\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Potential SQL string concatenation detected. Use parameterized queries.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        ),\\\\\\\\n        # TODO / FIXME additions\\\\\\\\n        (\\\\\\\\n            r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?i)^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\+.*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b