t does **not** satisfy R5.\\\\n\\\\n   **Disposition:** bind provenance to the retained condition through an opaque association or a witness authenticating its complete contents. Add token-transplant and modified-condition regressions.\\\\n\\\\n2. **P1 must-fix — ordinary caught exceptions now expose the envelope instead of the original exception.**  \\\\n   `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1536` includes `:yang.call/thrown` in the whole-condition retention branch at `:1545`. Catch lowering still exposes that whole map (`:1142`), while `rewrite-ex-info` still implements exception accessors as direct `:yin.k/message`/`:yin.k/data` lookups (`:915`).\\\\n\\\\n   Consequently, this public-call path statically yields `[nil nil]` instead of `[\\\\\\\"boom\\\\\\\" {:x 1}]`:\\\\n   ```clojure\\\\n   (let [f (fn [] (throw (ex-info \\\\\\\"boom\\\\\\\" {:x 1})))]\\\\n     (try (f)\\\\n          (catch Exception e [(ex-message e) (ex-data e)])))\\\\n   ```\\\\n   Direct intra-unit throws still expose the original payload, making ordinary catch behavior depend on routing. Whole-condition retention is necessary; changing the source-visible exception is not required by R3.\\\\n\\\\n   **Disposition:** preserve the original exception’s catching/accessor behavior while retaining the complete wire condition privately. Add a dynamic-call catch regression alongside the existing direct-throw tests.\\\\n\\\\n3. **P1 must-fix — retention can delete an original condition field.**  \\\\n   `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1546` overwrites any incoming `:dsg__condition` field. Both outbound strippers (`:1318`, `:2444`) then remove it. A genuinely transferred protocol condition containing that field as ordinary data therefore cannot be forwarded unchanged—even without source modification.\\\\n\\\\n   **Disposition:** store provenance outside the original condition, retaining the complete original map. Add a boundary fixture containing `:dsg__condition :ordinary-evidence` and assert exact preservation after immediate and saved rethrow.\\\\n\\\\n4. **P2 should-fix — two updated value-path assertions do not pin the required outer contract.**  \\\\n   `test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2620` and `:2637` inspect only the nested `:yang.call/not-callable` reason. Neither checks the outer `:yang.call/thrown` reason or callee evidence; the tail assertion also lacks an explicit error-tag check.\\\\n\\\\n   **Disposition:** assert the outer reason, error tag, inner reason, and callee evidence. The other three changed refusal expectations (`:2599`, `:2738`, `:2769`) already compare complete expected outcomes. All five wrapping changes are justified by ruling `1794332020000`; the concern is incomplete assertions, not the decision to wrap.\\\\n\\\\nThe six review questions resolve as follows:\\\\n\\\\n| Question | Assessment |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n| **1. R3 retention** | **Not clean:** original-field loss in finding 3. Ordinary marker-free protocol conditions follow the intended immediate/saved rethrow path; no additional double-transfer or after-call fallthrough found in the changed bridge. |\\\\n| **2. Provenance** | **Not clean:** finding 1. Mechanically, all six writers stamp `dsg__call_token`, and both readers use token equality; no truthiness reader remains. |\\\\n| **3. Top-outcome guard** | **Clean structurally:** vector/count checks precede indexing. Descriptor maps pass through. Ordinary guest two-vectors are inside successful outcomes and are not mistaken for the outer error outcome. Provenance remains subject to finding 1. |\\\\n| **4. Ordinary behavior/tests** | **Not clean:** finding 2 and assertion gap 4. Remaining large churn is indentation, plus the documented retention, stripping, and tail changes. |\\\\n| **5. Tail semantics** | **Clean statically:** `tails/remark-tails` runs at `:2685`, after all outcome wrappers and before annotation. No new path skips re-marking where the stripper is installed. |\\\\n| **6. Scope** | **Clean:** exactly the two authorized files and two specified commits. |\\\\n\\\\nREQUEST CHANGES\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"turn.completed\\\",\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":941098,\\\"cached_input_tokens\\\":846336,\\\"cache_write_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"output_tokens\\\":4691,\\\"reasoning_output_tokens\\\":1621}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/exception-track/1794365000000-reviewer-r3-identity-confirm.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git show c9c5533c:src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | nl -ba | sed -n '2380,2780p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-EkeOFTJX' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n2026-11-11 05:51:59.983 xcodebuild[63777:121393074]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\n2026-11-11 05:52:00.202 xcodebuild[63777:121393070] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\"Input/output error\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-x8VYtQXG' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n2026-11-11 05:52:00.995 xcodebuild[63787:121393109]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\n2026-11-11 05:52:01.180 xcodebuild[63787:121393105] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\"Input/output error\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\n  2380\\t\\n  2381\\t        ;; Special forms\\n  2382\\t        :else\\n  2383\\t        (case operator\\n  2384\\t          ;; Lambda: (fn [params] body)\\n  2385\\t          fn (if (::convention env)\\n  2386\\t               (