{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The heap field is the right storage, with two necessary amendments. GC currently traces only an entry’s `:value`, so it must also trace retained provenance—including for pinned wrappers. The raw Clojure source check rejects reserved door names, but macro output has a separate path that needs an admission check. Preserving the field on writes is sufficient; `cell/set!` need not refuse writes."}}
