{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | sed -n '1,140p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '1260,1314p;2820,2895p'; rg -n 'condition-wrapper-form|condition-retained-form|visible-of|witness|throw|condition' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | head -45; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1638,1686p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '4508,4540p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc | sed -n '1,100p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.clojure.prelude\n     2\t  \"The `clj` runtime module (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.10):\n     3\t   the published linker module every linked clojure program requires, as\n     4\t   `js`, `php` and `py` are for their frontends. It is written in prelude\n     5\t   notation and emitted with the same core machinery those preludes use;\n     6\t   it never runs on the host.\n     7\t\n     8\t   Three surfaces, mirroring the other runtimes:\n     9\t\n    10\t   - the entry, `clj/run-main`: initialize the runtime state, run the\n    11\t     unit — the thunk `yang.clojure/lower-unit` lowered — and answer the\n    12\t     program's value with the outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]`\n    13\t     wrapper removed, since that wrapper is frontend-internal. The\n    14\t     entry does not reset the global namespace: the namespace lives for\n    15\t     the task, so a projection the composition bound between two\n    16\t     entries and a definition an earlier unit published both survive\n    17\t     into the next unit's run (as `js/run-main` leaves `globalThis`\n    18\t     standing);\n    19\t   - the runtime global namespace, `clj/define-global!` and\n    20\t     `clj/global-get`: a task-local map in a cell (`clj.rt/globals`,\n    21\t     allocated once per task by `clj/init!`), keyed by export name. A\n    22\t     program's top-level definitions land here through its unit's own\n    23\t     publishing, and the conformance helper's export projection reads\n    24\t     and writes it — the one binding a linked unit reads a projected or\n    25\t     defined name through. A definition a unit runs publishes after\n    26\t     any projection of the same name and shadows it. The JS\n    27\t     `globalThis` table, the PHP named-function table and the Python\n    28\t     module dictionary are the same seam;\n    29\t   - admission, `admit`: the registry surface a linked clojure composition\n    30\t     needs beside the others — the `kind` module and the `portable`\n    31\t     adapters of the data exports the guest library's collection\n    32\t     predicates read.\n    33\t\n    34\t   The module pins the shared calling runtime (`yang.call`) at the\n    35\t   convention's call-address, as the other runtimes do, and refuses before\n    36\t   anything is published when a free name nothing supplies is read.\"\n    37\t  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n    38\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n    39\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    40\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    41\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(def module-name\n    45\t  \"The linker module name of the clojure runtime.\"\n    46\t  'clj)\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(def runtime-keys\n    50\t  \"Every runtime key, each with an `:clj/uninit` placeholder at module\n    51\t   level so every read is discharged before `clj/init!` allocates the\n    52\t   real cell. They stay qualified: internal store keys, never guest\n    53\t   names.\"\n    54\t  '[clj.rt/state clj.rt/globals])\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t(def definitions\n    58\t  \"The module's definition list, in prelude notation (the module's own\n    59\t   `clj/` prefix is stripped on emit).\"\n    60\t  '[;; ------------------------------------------------- state and namespace\n    61\t    [clj/init!\n    62\t     (fn []\n    63\t       (if (= clj.rt/state :clj/uninit)\n    64\t         (do (yin/def (quote clj.rt/globals) (cell/new {}))\n    65\t             (yin/def (quote clj.rt/state) :clj/ready))\n    66\t         :clj/ready))]\n    67\t    ;; the runtime global namespace: one task-local map in a cell, keyed by\n    68\t    ;; export name. `clj/define-global!` answers the value, so a publish\n    69\t    ;; sequence can chain through it.\n    70\t    [clj/define-global!\n    71\t     (fn [name value]\n    72\t       (do (cell/set! clj.rt/globals\n    73\t                      (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name value))\n    74\t           value))]\n    75\t    [clj/global-get\n    76\t     (fn [name]\n    77\t       (if (data/contains? (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n    78\t         (get (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n    79\t         :clj/unbound))]\n    80\t\n    81\t    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- entry\n    82\t    ;; The outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]` wrapper is frontend-\n    83\t    ;; internal, so the entry removes one wrapper level from the\n    84\t    ;; program's value (a program returning that vector as data was\n    85\t    ;; wrapped again, so one level is exact). An error outcome passes\n    86\t    ;; through as the failure value for the caller to render.\n    87\t    [clj/unwrap-outcome\n    88\t     (fn [value]\n    89\t       (if (if (data/vector? value) (= (data/count value) 2) false)\n    90\t         (if (= (data/nth value 0) :yin.k/ok)\n    91\t           (data/nth value 1)\n    92\t           value)\n    93\t         value))]\n    94\t    ;; The global namespace is the task's, not the entry's: no reset\n    95\t    ;; here, so projections and earlier units' definitions survive.\n    96\t    [clj/run-main\n    97\t     (fn [body]\n    98\t       (do (clj/init!)\n    99\t           (clj/unwrap-outcome (body))))]])\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(def module-definitions\n   103\t  \"The module's definition list: an