{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show e735ebb2:src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | nl -ba | sed -n '908,1003p;1390,1418p;1620,1698p;2480,2518p'; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show e735ebb2:docs/agents/known-gaps.md | nl -ba | tail -38; rg -n '3878|3885|8.10.7|identity.*lifetime|retained|source.writable' docs/design/yang.antlr.md | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"   908\t;; =============================================================================\n   909\t;;\n   910\t;; An ORDINARY `:yang.call/thrown` payload crosses a call site RAW: the\n   911\t;; error-outcome slot carries the payload itself, so the caught value IS\n   912\t;; the payload and every guest observation (equality in any position, map\n   913\t;; keys, count, assoc, truthiness, predicates under any spelling, passage\n   914\t;; to another unit) is correct by construction, with no compiler routing.\n   915\t;; No wrapper, no retention: the wire condition is reconstructible from\n   916\t;; the payload as a fresh `:yang.call/thrown` at the public boundary.\n   917\t;;\n   918\t;; The wrapper survives ONLY as clojure's documented local form for\n   919\t;; QUALIFIED protocol conditions (`:yang.call/not-callable`,\n   920\t;; `:invalid-invocation`, `:unsupported-binding`): a task-owned cell whose\n   921\t;; contents are [visible condition], minted through the issuer-only\n   922\t;; retained mint (`cell/dsg__new-retained`, a name guest source cannot\n   923\t;; spell). Retention is bound to heap identity, not contents: the engine\n   924\t;; marks the wrapper's heap entry `:retained`, `cell/set!` refuses marked\n   925\t;; entries (contents frozen for the wrapper's lifetime), and the pure\n   926\t;; `cell/retained?` query answers from the heap, so a guest copy of the\n   927\t;; contents in a fresh cell decodes as an ordinary payload, never as a\n   928\t;; retained condition. The association is the cell's identity, so saving\n   929\t;; and returning the wrapper works, and so does a rethrow from another\n   930\t;; activation. Decoding reads cell contents and never applies a guest\n   931\t;; value.\n   932\t\n   933\t(def ^:private visible-of-form\n   934\t  '(fn [dsg__value]\n   935\t     (if (data/map? dsg__value)\n   936\t       (let [dsg__decoded (dsg__condition_retained dsg__value)]\n   937\t         (if (dsg__equal dsg__decoded nil)\n   938\t           dsg__value\n   939\t           (data/nth dsg__decoded 0)))\n   940\t       dsg__value)))\n   941\t\n   942\t\n   943\t(def ^:private condition-wrapper-form\n   944\t  '(fn [dsg__visible dsg__condition]\n   945\t     (cell/dsg__new-retained\n   946\t       (conj (conj [] dsg__visible) dsg__condition))))\n   947\t\n   948\t\n   949\t(def ^:private condition-retained-form\n   950\t  '(fn [dsg__candidate]\n   951\t     (if (data/map? dsg__candidate)\n   952\t       (if (dsg__equal (dsg__get dsg__candidate :type) :cell-ref)\n   953\t         (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate :id)\n   954\t           (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate :seal)\n   955\t             (if (data/string? (dsg__get dsg__candidate :seal))\n   956\t               (if (dsg__equal (data/str-length (dsg__get dsg__candidate :seal)) 64)\n   957\t                 (if (cell/retained? dsg__candidate)\n   958\t                   (let [dsg__contents (cell/get dsg__candidate)]\n   959\t                     (if (data/vector? dsg__contents)\n   960\t                       (if (dsg__equal (data/count dsg__contents) 2)\n   961\t                         (conj (conj [] (data/nth dsg__contents 0))\n   962\t                               (data/nth dsg__contents 1))\n   963\t                         nil)\n   964\t                       nil))\n   965\t                   nil)\n   966\t                 nil)\n   967\t               nil)\n   968\t             nil)\n   969\t           nil)\n   970\t         nil)\n   971\t       nil)))\n