..)`) is a syntax error in the vendored `PhpParser.g4` (an argument list has no bare `...`); `Closure::fromCallable` and the callable forms (`[$o, 'm']`, `'A::m'`, invokable objects) carry the semantics | P4 S6; `antlr/php/PhpParser.g4` `arguments` | yang.php | a grammar patch slice before P4 S10 (php-src selection uses the syntax) | P3 |\n   576\t| yang.php: the `callable` type check (`php/callable?`) sees only public methods, because a type check has no calling scope; a private `[$this, 'm']` callable passed to a `callable` parameter from inside its class is rejected, while calling it directly works; closure rebinding does not warn for the unbind-`$this` and internal-class cases, and `static` is accepted only as a return type (as a parameter or property type it never matches) | P4 S6 | yang.php | P4 S10 (departure fixtures from the object permutation alphabet) | P3 |\n   577\t| yang.php: destructuring by reference into a property (`[&$o->p] = $a`, row 47) is not lowered: the destructuring pattern accepts variable and element targets only; fixture `:obj-row47-destructure-by-ref-into-typed-property` is authored and gated by `:p4-row47` | checkpoint B audit (fixture package); `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc` `pattern-of` | yang.php | P4 S7 or a destructuring slice before checkpoint C (the gate lifts when the pattern accepts property targets) | P2 |\n   578\t| yang.php: `exit`/`die` is refused (`:constant`), so row 51 (`exit` inside a destructor proceeds to shutdown, corner C9) cannot run; fixture `:obj-row51-exit-in-destructor` is authored and gated by `:p4-exit` | checkpoint B audit (fixture package); design row 51 | yang.php | P4 S7 (the exit escape and the pending-exception destruct halt) | P2 |\n   579\t| yang.php: a direct write to a typed static property (`A::$s = 'x'`) is not type-checked; only a reference to it is (a source keyed by class and property, row 46), so assignment through the reference is checked and the direct assignment is not | checkpoint B 