{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794371000000-reviewer-r3-A-design-confirm.glm-5.3.findings.md | sed -n '70,105p;128,181p'; nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794341000000-continuation-orchestrator-unification-ruling-of-record.md | sed -n '1,135p'; nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794343000000-exception-track-surface-registry.md | sed -n '1,135p'; nl -ba test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj | sed -n '100,143p'\"","aggregated_output":"    70\tEvery entry in the brief's table answers the payload. The seven round-3 observation\n    71\tleaks are closed by construction (`e` IS the payload; the per-call-site router is gone —\n    72\t`visible-all-operands-ops` deleted, `visible-predicate-heads` deleted, only `get` keeps\n    73\tvisible-routing for the protocol wrapper's accessors).\n    74\t\n    75\t## Reviewer-added seam probes (Part-2 evidence, both lanes)\n    76\t\n    77\t- P12 `(cell/retained? {:type :cell-ref :id :cell-999999 :seal <64 chars>})` on\n    78\t  ref-shaped DATA: `false`, non-fatal — the query answers from the heap, fail-safe\n    79\t  against the forged-map residual from the r4 ruling.\n    80\t- P13 GC: 5000 `cell/new` allocations (threshold 4096 → ≥1 stop-the-world collection)\n    81\t  while a wrapper is saved: `(cell/retained? wrapper)` = `true` after, contents intact\n    82\t  (`:yang.call/not-callable` readable). **The `:retained` mark survives `sweep`** — the\n    83\t  one place heap entries are rebuilt operates on whole entries.\n    84\t- P14 guest source `(cell/dsg__new-retained :x)`: refused at compile —\n    85\t  `\"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\" {:symbol cell/dsg__new-retained,\n    86\t  :prefix \"dsg__\"}`. The pre-pass (`check-program-symbols!`, clojure.cljc:2511) refuses\n    87\t  the prefix in ANY unquoted position including qualified heads; def names likewise.\n    88\t- P15 a QUOTED dsg symbol is inert data (travels as data, no compile of its shape).\n    89\t- P16 a guest `defmacro` whose body returns a dsg-headed form: on this round's lanes the\n    90\t  call runs as an ordinary function returning data — no expansion path exists under\n    91\t  `compile-program`, so no injection. (See Part-2 caveat 3.)\n    92\t\n    93\t# Part 2 — adjudication of the VM scope expansion\n    94\t\n    95\t## Verdict: the seam is technically SAFE; the authorization is NEEDS-OWNER. The clojure-side work is fully separable and can land without the VM change.\n    96\t\n    97\t### 1. Invariants — no breakage found (static + empirical)\n    98\t\n    99\t- **Heap-entry shape**: the mark is an extra key in the heap ENTRY (`{:value v :seal s\n   100\t  :retained true}`), never in the value. No consumer rebuilds entries from `{:value\n   101\t  :seal}` pairs: `sweep` dissocs whole entries, `trace`/`mark` read `:value` only,\n   102\t  `debruijn/{register,stack}` carry `:heap` whole, `ast_walker` threads it positionally.\n   103\t  dao.stream/UCF/lift never touch `:heap` (grep across src/cljc: only yin.vm files).\n   104\t  Empirically: `yin.vm.cell-test` + `heap-reclamation-test` + `module-test` +\n   105\t  `effect-forgery-test` = 48 tests/521 assertions green; `engine/ast-walker/\n   128\t### 3. Module surface reachability\n   129\t\n   130\t- The MINT `cell/dsg__new-retained` is unreachable from guest source: refused by the\n   131\t  source pre-pass (P14, any unquoted position, qualified heads included); other yang\n   132\t  compilers (python/php/typescript/core) emit a FIXED cell vocabulary\n   133\t  (`cell/new`, `cell/get`, `cell/set!`, `cell/authentic?` only — grep) with no\n   134\t  guest-controlled `cell/NAME` pass-through. Caveat, pre-existing, not introduced here:\n   135\t  the macro/row pipeline (`yin.vm.macro`, Rule R) reserves only `yin/def`, so IF a guest\n   136\t  macro expansion could carry a dsg_-headed form into compiled code the mint would\n   137\t  resolve (module-qualified variables resolve by registry lookup). The same exposure\n   138\t  existed at c9c5533c for `dsg__condition_wrapper`, so the class is unchanged — but the\n   139\t  (A) design's \"issuer-only mint\" claim should get one follow-up probe on the\n   140\t  macro/REPL lane before the owner signs the VM surface (recommend as an S2 item, not a\n   141\t  blocker for this round's lanes).\n   142\t- The QUERY `cell/retained?` is deliberately guest-reachable in yang.clojure (mirrors\n   143\t  `authentic?`, used by the committed battery's own guest code); it discloses only\n   144\t  heap-issued carrier status — information the guest already has via reason/data reads.\n   145\t  It is NOT exposed by the other dialects (they never emit it).\n   146\t\n   147\t### 4. Track scope — the precise owner question\n   148\t\n   149\tThe mob's (A) — as I authored it and qwen concurred structurally — included the heap\n   150\tmark as commitment #3, and the seat's mob record dispatches the implementation to\n   151\t\"satisfy the probes, not pick a citation\"; muse-wonder implemented the glm variant\n   152\tfaithfully. But the track's written authorization names the (B) fallback, and a change\n   153\tto `yin/vm/engine.cljc` + the shared `cell-module` surface crosses the yang.clojure →\n   154\tyin.vm boundary that other tracks (dao.stream, linker, UCF) sit on. That is an owner\n   155\truling, not a reviewer's to make. **The ruling should ask exactly this**: may the cell\n   156\tmodule publish an issuer-side retained mint (`dsg__new-retained`) + query (`retained?`)\n   157\tand may `:cell/set!` refuse heap-marked cells.\n   158\t\n   159\t**Separability: YES.** The raw-payload half — the part that closes all seven observation\n   160\tleaks and restores the Round-0 green rows — is entirely in `condition->outcome`\n   161\t(thrown-arm and unqualified-arm deliver the payload) plus the router deletion; it has no\n   162\tVM dependency. Only `condition-wrapper-form`/`condition-retained-form` (the protocol\n   163\twrapper's mint and decoder) use the new surface; reverting those two forms to the\n   164\tc9c5533c witness versions yields raw ordinary payloads + witnessed protocol retention\n   165\twith zero VM change, if the owner declines. The cost of declining is the witness's\n   166\tcontents-volume (three slots, closure-carrying) versus the mark's two.\n   167\t\n   168\t## Minor findings (non-blocking)\n   169\t\n   170\t1. **P3, docs**: `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:119` still documents `:heap` as\n   171\t   `{cell-id {:value v :seal s}}`; the mark makes the entry shape\n   172\t   `{:value v :seal s :retained? true}`. One line, fold into the owner round.\n   173\t2. **P3, dead clause**: `heap-write`'s mark-preservation is unreachable today (see 2.3);\n   174\t   keep or comment, but worth a note in the ledger.\n   175\t3. **S2, macro-lane probe**: the dsg__ regime's strength on the yin.vm.macro expansion\n   176\t   lane is unprobed (out of this round's lanes; exposure class unchanged from c9c5533c).\n   177\t4. **Not run**: cljs (shadow-cljs node) and cljd (flutter) lanes — engine.cljc changes\n   178\t   are plain cljc with no reader/ host divergence, but the lanes were not exercised in\n   179\t   this round; kondo/cljstyle not run (read-only round). Fast JVM lanes above are the\n   180\t   evidence base.\n   181\t\n     1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-10 19:58:00 GMT\n     2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 02:58:00 +07 (+0700)\n     3\tCoding-Agent: interactive (ZCode / glm-5.3-flash, continuation-semantics orchestrator seat)\n     4\tSession-ID: not-applicable (interactive seat)\n     5\tStatus: OWNER-DECIDED 2026-11-11 02:5x +07 (in-session, verbatim below); seat-filed 03:0x +07\n     6\tOwner decision, verbatim answer to the seat's structured question (\"which bar must the track meet?\"):\n     7\t> \"(A) now, (B) if R4 proof fails\" — Sign (A) now; clojure moves to continuation lowering only if\n     8\t> its R4 equivalence proof fails (the pre-authorized fallback). Decides later on evidence instead\n     9\t> of paying (B)'s cost upfront.\n    10\tConsequences as filed below stand, amended: the ts/php hold LIFTS on this decision (premise\n    11\t\"the unification track completes\" is satisfied — the unification question is answered (A)); R4's\n    12\tscope is confirmed per (1) with the (B) fallback now OWNER-AUTHORIZED, not merely pre-registered;\n    13\titem (2)'s \"dispatch remains parked until the owner's word\" is superseded by this word.\n    14\t\n    15\t# RULING OF RECORD (proposed) — the internal-exception-encoding unification question\n    16\t\n    17\t## The question\n    18\t\n    19\tShould the exception track go beyond ruling v2's boundary uniformity\n    20\t(`collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md`) and converge the\n    21\tINTERNAL exception encodings of the four frontends — and if so, on which encoding?\n    22\t\n    23\t## The seat's finding: mob consensus 3/3 for (A) — keep v2 as-is\n    24\t\n    25\tThree independent architect rulings, dispatched in parallel on identical briefs\n    26\t(`179433838900{0,1,2}-architect-outcome-vs-continuation-unification.prompt.md`), each ruling from\n    27\tits own file:line evidence:\n    28\t\n    29\t1. **argon** (gemini-4-argon-high, agy, conversation `cdc97c9b-ce7e-438e-8044-87aeab3c725d`):\n    30\t   **(A)**. Decisive mechanics: the `%capture`-based `try` makes its body structurally non-tail\n    31\t   (`u/let1` lowers `(let [v (body)] (restore! saved) v)` — body is an operand, `tail? false`, one\n    32\t   CESK frame per try execution), which destroys slice-5's constant-depth property; porting\n    33\t   py/ts/php onto outcome tuples violates §8.10.7's normal-return invariant (\"no completion packet\n    34\t   around each result\") across 14,100+ prelude lines that still need `%capture` for\n    35\t   finally/break/continue/with/generators regardless. Cataloged FIVE real semantic differences\n    36\t   among the three try families (try arity, frame width, restore! semantics, empty-stack policy,\n    37\t   terminal escapes), rejecting premature dedup. Novel obligation: R4b must test cross-unit\n    38\t   clojure callables (`clojure->clojure` across units, `clojure->python->clojure`) so\n    39\t   `dsg__admitted?` and `:clj/outcomes?` cannot disagree across token segments.\n    40\t   Log: `1794338389000-...gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log`.\n    41\t\n    42\t2. **astra** (gpt-6-astra, codex): **(A)**. \"The code supports keeping v2.\" Clojure has explicit\n    43\t   constant-depth regression tests (`test-outcome-common-call-depth`); outcome retention is\n    44\t   conditional on R4's proof, not grandfathered.\n    45\t   Log: `1794338389001-...gpt-6-astra.stdout.log`.\n    46\t\n    47\t3. **deepseek-flash** (deepseek CLI, session `99b84f47-8b92-431e-b93f-9efc1cdcb63d`): **(A)**.\n    48\t   Decisive observation: no internal convergence flips a single currently-red acceptance row —\n    49\t   every red row is a boundary bridge/reception defect. The §8.10.7 boundary transfer is the only\n    50\t   integration surface; flags that the ts/php hold relay's \"unify exceptions as yin.vm\n    51\t   continuations\" is an orchestrator paraphrase, and only the owner can supersede v2 if the owner\n    52\t   meant a forced internal encoding.\n    53\t   Log: `1794338389002-...deepseek-4.1-flash.stdout.log` (provenance note in the prompt header:\n    54\t   the literal name `deepseek-4.1-flash` was rejected by the endpoint with 400; the flash lane is\n    55\t   `deepseek-flash`).\n    56\t\n    57\tAll three verdicts are mutually consistent and consistent with ruling v2 and the three R3-arc\n    58\tadjudications (1794320926000, 1794332020000, 1794336505000).\n    59\t\n    60\t## The ruling this seat files (per the mob, for the owner's signature)\n    61\t\n    62\t**(A) — v2 stands.** Boundary uniformity only: the §8.10.7 condition\n    63\t`{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value v}` at every admitted guest-call boundary\n    64\tis the entirety of the required uniformity. yang.clojure keeps its internal outcome encoding\n    65\tCONDITIONAL on R4's equivalence proof at the §8.10.9 bar (not grandfathered); py/ts/php keep their\n    66\tcontinuation-handler preludes. There is no \"unify the internals\" work item, and the\n    67\t\"unify exceptions as yin.vm continuations\" phrase in the ts/php hold relay means the boundary\n    68\ttransfer, not a forced internal representation.\n    69\t\n    70\t## Consequences this seat derives\n    71\t\n    72\t1. **R4 scope** (unification bounds it): R4 proves the outcome channel EQUIVALENT to the\n    73\t   raise-exit lane at the §8.10.9 bar (caught/uncaught/protocol-rethrow/binding/higher-order, the\n    74\t   pre-registered `:clojure-private-public-equivalence` obligation) — plus argon's cross-unit\n    75\t   callable scenarios. On failure, the pre-authorized fallback is unifying clojure onto the\n    76\t   raise-exit lane (no new owner license needed).\n    77\t2. **ts/php hold** (this seat's call, per the handoff): the hold's premise was \"the unification\n    78\t   track completes.\" Under (A), the unification question is now answered — the track's work IS\n    79\t   v2's boundary sequencing. The hold is LIFTED once the owner signs this ruling; JS R1+R3\n    80\t   resumes as v2's first round. Dispatch remains parked until the owner's word.\n    81\t3. **Deferred (optional, post-R1/R2/R3)**: deduplication of the triplicated py/js/php try-family\n    82\t   into one parameterized core prelude + one cross-frontend isomorphism test — a refactor round,\n    83\t   NOT convergence; must parameterize argon's five documented differences and land after the\n    84\t   boundary rounds (deepseek's sequencing caution).\n    85\t4. **Not authorized by this ruling**: any change to internal encodings in any frontend; any\n    86\t   shared-prelude work before R1-R3 land.\n    87\t\n    88\t## Owner decision requested\n    89\t\n    90\tConfirm or amend: (a) sign (A) as the ruling of record; (b) lift the ts/php hold per (2); (c)\n    91\tconfirm R4's scope per (1).\n     1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-10 20:35:00 GMT\n     2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 03:35:00 +07 (+0700)\n     3\tCoding-Agent: interactive (ZCode / glm-5.3-flash, continuation-semantics orchestrator seat)\n     4\tSession-ID: not-applicable (interactive seat)\n     5\tStatus: ACTIVE — the ownership registry of record for the exception track\n     6\t\n     7\t# Exception track — ceded-surfaces registry & coordination rules\n     8\t\n     9\tAuthority: owner ruling v2 (1794960000000), owner decision 2026-11-11 \"(A) now, (B) if R4 proof\n    10\tfails\" (1794341000000). The ts/php dispatch hold is LIFTED. No track-level pause of any yang.*\n    11\tseat: serialization is FILE-LEVEL only, on the surfaces below.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Registry — surfaces owned exclusively by the exception track (until the round lands)\n    14\t\n    15\t| Frontend | Ceded surface (files + regions) | Owning round | Status |\n    16\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n    17\t| typescript (js) | `typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc` entry bridge (`:1581` region) + protocol-condition paths (`:1627` region) + reception; kit test surfaces under `test/yang/call/` | JS R1+R3 (relay 1794970001000) | IN FLIGHT — branch `exception-js-r1r3` @ master 4cfa609d, worktree datomworld-jsr13, muse-spark-1.3-contributor session B1FBBBB5-52A0-42A2-BAFC-9742A463A51C (ts seat dispatch note 1794346200000) |\n    18\t| php | `php/antlr/prelude.cljc` function entry (`:2264`), Closure entry (`:4217`), `php/call`/`call-with-binding-profile`/`call-named`, ForeignException reception, protocol rethrow (`:194-197`, `:2384`, `:4085` regions); kit test surfaces | PHP R1+R2+R3 (one coherent round) | STAGED — brief 1794342800000 filed; dispatch gated on JS R1+R3 landing (php seat ack 1794342949000) |\n    19\t| python | `pytho