   37\t\n    38\tRule: a round from any other track that would edit one of these files' listed regions queues\n    39\tbehind the owning round (one-writer, per file+region). Everything else in every frontend\n    40\tproceeds normally, in its own worktree. Any frontend round's G0/G1 verification includes the\n    41\tkit namespaces (`yang.call.exception-contract-test`) — a flip in any row you did not author\n    42\tstops the round for diagnosis.\n    43\t\n    44\t## Branch registry (prevents the r3-style ambiguity)\n    45\t\n    46\t- `exception-r0` — landed (master 0fa3ff7a). CLOSED.\n    47\t- `exception-r3-impl` — owned by THIS seat (continuation-semantics orchestrator); worktree\n    48\t  `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch`. IN FLIGHT.\n    49\t- `exception-r3` — EMPTY/stale, created by nobody current; do not use; delete only on owner word.\n    50\t- Planned: `exception-js-r1r3` (ts/php seat), `exception-php-r1r2r3` (ts/php seat),\n    51\t  `exception-py-r2r3` (python seat), `exception-r4` (this seat). Cut each from current master at\n    52\t  round start; one writer per branch; never cut a round on another seat's branch.\n    53\t\n    54\t## Conditional pause trigger\n    55\t\n    56\tIf R4's equivalence proof fails, the owner-authorized (B) fallback rewrites clojure.cljc broadly;\n    57\tat that point ALL yang.clojure rounds pause until the fallback lands and its gates re-verify.\n    58\tNo other frontend pauses (it changes clojure's internal encoding only, not the boundary contract).\n    59\t\n    60\t## AMENDMENT (2026-11-11 23:2x +07) — the VM provenance round (owner-authorized; steward takes round ownership)\n    61\t\n    62\tOwner authorized (via the python seat's relay, handoff `1794450000000-crosslang-handoff-vm-provenance.md`)\n    63\ta bounded VM change: **private per-sealed-entry provenance storage** — a host-only sibling field on\n    64\theap entries (proposed `:yang.call/provenance`), write-once at wrapper mint via a reserved-prefix\n    65\tdoor, host-identity read via a reserved query, GC-with-entry, no guest-visible vocabulary beyond the\n    66\treserved doors (if public surface must change: full `cell/authentic?` rigor + architect second\n    67\topinion).\n    68\t\n    69\t- **Round owner**: the continuation-semantics orchestrator (this seat). Branch: `exception-vm-provenance`,\n    70\t  cut from current master, touching ONLY `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc` + `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc`\n    71\t  (+ their tests). **This CLAIMS the yin.vm heap-entry surface for that round** — the yin.vm seat is\n    72\t  notified here per the queue rule; contention = coordinate before writing.\n    73\t- **Acceptance contract** (committed RED): `exception-py-r2r3` @ `0326a044`,\n    74\t  `test/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj` forgery pins — do not rewrite, they are the contract.\n    75\t- **Adoption sequence**: python wires its wrapper mint/read onto the primitive (its seat, on\n    76\t  `exception-py-r2r3`); php adopts at its round's start; **the clojure port consumes it for\n    77\t  protocol-condition retention** (replacing the witness + its documented replay/mutation hole —\n    78\t  the port brief is amended accordingly); **js is GRANDFATHERED** (its `js.rt` identity store is\n    79\t  sound and shipped; migration optional, non-urgent).\n    80\t- **Precondition**: the engineer/architect design consult (owner condition (a)) and the\n    81\t  cross-frontend ruling (condition (b)) — dispatched as\n    82\t  `1794451000000-consult-vm-provenance-design.prompt.md`.\n    83\t- Note of record: the earlier NO on the VM seam declined the OUTCOME-encoding wrapper's compensation;\n    84\t  this primitive is the uniform R3-contract mechanism for the continuation encoding's four frontends\n    85\t  — different character, owner-authorized through the python seat's brief.\n    86\t- Also amended: the clojure registry claim above widens to the whole `clojure.cljc` (+ `clojure/prelude.cljc`)\n    87\t  for the convergence port (`exception-r3-impl` extends the R3 bridge work; not re-cut from master).\n   100\t  (vec\n   101\t    (concat\n   102\t      (for [f (sort frontends), kind [:named :closure]]\n   103\t        (fixture (keyword (str \"fresh-\" (name kind))) f #{::r1 ::r5}\n   104\t                 {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   105\t                  :reason :yang.call/thrown :payload-identical true}\n   106\t                 {:callable-kind kind}))\n   107\t      (for [f [:clojure :php :python]]\n   108\t        (fixture :binding f #{::r1} {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   109\t                                     :reason :yang.call/thrown}))\n   110\t      (for [f (sort frontends), reason protocol-reasons]\n   111\t        (fixture (keyword (str \"protocol-\" (name reason))) f #{::r3}\n   112\t                 {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   113\t                  :condition-identical true :reason reason}\n   114\t                 {:protocol-reason reason}))\n   115\t      (for [f [:python :php]]\n   116\t        (fixture :local-reception f #{::r2}\n   117\t                 {:returned true :payload-identical true}))\n   118\t      (for [f [:python :php]]\n   119\t        (fixture :foreign-reception f #{::r2}\n   120\t                 {:returned true :local-foreign-exception true}))\n   121\t      (for [f [:python :php]]\n   122\t        (fixture :retained-foreign-lifetime f #{::r2 ::r5}\n   123\t                 {:retained true :local-foreign-exception true\n   124\t                  :transferred true :once true :after false\n   125\t                  :condition-identical true :payload-identical true}))\n   126\t      (for [f (sort frontends), reason protocol-reasons]\n   127\t        (fixture (keyword (str \"saved-protocol-\" (name reason))) f #{::r3 ::r5}\n   128\t                 {:retained true :transferred true :once true :after false\n   129\t                  :condition-identical true :reason reason}\n   130\t                 {:protocol-reason reason}))\n   131\t      (for [f [:clojure :typescript], scenario [:shape-return :shape-throw]]\n   132\t        (fixture scenario f #{::r5}\n   133\t                 (if (= scenario :shape-return)\n   134\t                   {:returned true :payload-identical true}\n   135\t                   {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   136\t                    :reason :yang.call/thrown :payload-identical true})))\n   137\t      (for [f [:python :php]]\n   138\t        (fixture :forged-retention f #{::r5}\n   139\t                 {:transferred true :once true :after false\n   140\t                  :reason :yang.call/thrown :payload-identical true})))))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(def pair-scenarios\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
