{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\\\\[py/make-exc|\\\\[py/make-instance|\\\\[php/make-error|\\\\[php/new-object|defn-.*error|\\\\[js/make-error' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '2685,2722p;2804,2826p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md | sed -n '104,133p'; nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794371000000-reviewer-r3-A-design-confirm.glm-5.3.findings.md | sed -n '105,127p'; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff --stat; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show --stat --oneline 0326a044\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1841:    [js/make-error\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:744:    [py/make-instance\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:748:    [py/make-exc\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:299:    [php/make-error\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:307:    [php/make-error-map\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5715:(defn- error-exception-members\n  2685\t(defn handle-effect\n  2686\t  \"Dispatch an effect and return {:state updated-state :value v :blocked? bool}.\n  2687\t   park-entry-fns maps :stream/put and :stream/next to functions that build\n  2688\t   wait entries.\n  2689\t\n  2690\t   `effect` must be a `yin.vm.effect` value minted by `module/make-effect`\n  2691\t   (D4); a map, whatever its keys, is data and is refused here.\n  2692\t\n  2693\t   A parked entry is stored as the builder left it plus, for a writer, the\n  2694\t   `:datom` it retries: registers and resource ids only. Neither the live\n  2695\t   stream handle nor a restore closure is attached — `check-wait-set`\n  2696\t   resolves handles from `:resources` at every poll, and the scheduler that pops\n  2697\t   a woken entry dispatches restoration itself — so a blocked entry is pure\n  2698\t   data and survives serialization.\"\n  2699\t  [state effect {:keys [park-entry-fns], :as opts}]\n  2700\t  (when-not (module/effect? effect)\n  2701\t    (fail \"Not an effect\" {:reason :not-an-effect}))\n  2702\t  (let [park-entry (get park-entry-fns (:effect effect))\n  2703\t        result\n  2704\t        (case (:effect effect)\n  2705\t          :vm/store-put {:state (put-active state\n  2706\t                                            (store-context state)\n  2707\t                                            (:key effect)\n  2708\t                                            (:val effect)),\n  2709\t                         :value (:val effect),\n  2710\t                         :blocked? false}\n  2711\t          :stream/make\n  2712\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"stream\")\n  2713\t                [stream-ref new-state] (handle-make s' effect id)]\n  2714\t            {:state new-state, :value stream-ref, :blocked? false})\n  2715\t          :stream/cursor\n  2716\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \"cursor\")\n  2717\t                [cursor-ref new-state]\n  2718\t                (case (gate-refuse! state effect)\n  2719\t                  :running\n  2720\t                  (handle-cursor-unminted s' effect id (or (:id-counter state) 0))\n  2721\t                  (handle-cursor s' effect id))]\n  2722\t            {:state new-state, :value cursor-ref, :blocked? false})\n  2804\t              (handler s' effect (assoc opts :id id))\n  2805\t              (fail \"Unknown effect\" {:effect (:effect effect)}))))]\n  2806\t    (update result\n  2807\t            :state\n  2808\t            (fn [result-state]\n  2809\t              (telemetry/emit-snapshot (assoc result-state\n  2810\t                                              :value (:value result))\n  2811\t                                       :effect\n  2812\t                                       {:effect-type (:effect effect)})))))\n  2813\t\n  2814\t\n  2815\t;; =============================================================================\n  2816\t;; Program Cache Machinery\n  2817\t;; =============================================================================\n  2818\t\n  2819\t(def default-compiled-cache-limit 8)\n  2820\t\n  2821\t\n  2822\t(defn build-program-index\n  2823\t  [datoms]\n  2824\t  (group-by first (vec datoms)))\n  2825\t\n  2826\t\n   104\t```clojure\n   105\t;; Store with allocated memory\n   106\t{:store {0 42           ; address 0 contains 42\n   107\t         1 \"hello\"      ; address 1 contains \"hello\"\n   108\t         2 [1 2 3]}}    ; address 2 contains vector\n   109\t```\n   110\t\n   111\t### `:owner` - The Task's Owner Tag\n   112\t\n   113\t**Type:** a string, or nil\n   114\t\n   115\t**Purpose:** The owner tag every closure and continuation this task mints carries (D7), derived once from the capability secret by `yin.vm.values/owner-tag` in `yin.vm/empty-state` and never revealing it. A task composed without a secret has owner nil. Application and invocation refuse a closure or continuation whose owner is not this task's (`:foreign-value`); the lift encoder refuses one as `:yin.k/non-portable`, and `lower-closure` mints with the receiver's owner. Cell, stream and cursor references are not owner-tagged: they stay sealed plain data.\n   116\t\n   117\t### `:heap` and `:gc` - Task Heap and Its Collector\n   118\t\n   119\t**Type:** `:heap` is `{cell-id {:value v :seal s}}`; `:gc` is `{:since n :base b :threshold t :pinned #{cell-id}}`\n   120\t\n   121\t**Purpose:** `:heap` holds the task's cells, the mutable locations `cell/new` allocates and a sealed `:cell-ref` reaches. It is VM state, not continuation state: a write is seen by every holder of the ref and survives continuation re-entry (box semantics). `:gc` is its collector's state. Both are declared record fields wherever a VM is a positional record, and both start empty in every constructor and `spawn-module` child.\n   122\t\n   123\t**Reclamation:** deterministic, allocation-triggered, stop-the-world mark-sweep, tracing kernel positions and value positions in two modes (`ast.md` Part 6),, a pure `vm -> vm'` (`yin.vm.engine/collect`). `:since` counts allocations; when it reaches `:threshold`, the `:cell/new` effect collects before allocating, and the threshold becomes `max(:base, 2 x live)`. `:base` is a composition parameter (`:gc-threshold`, default 4096). Marking runs over the heap as it was when the cycle began, and the sweep removes only ids of that snapshot, so an id allocated at or after the cycle's counter start is spared; a budgeted marker can later reuse it. `:pinned` holds cells whose refs left the VM's view on a stream or in an FFI request; they stay live for the task's life. Ids are never reused (`:id-counter` only grows), and a ref to a swept cell is refused with `:dead-or-forged-reference`. This supersedes the cell ruling's \"heap reclamation can wait\".\n   124\t\n   125\t### `:continuation` - Return Context\n   126\t\n   127\t**Type:** Continuation map or `nil`\n   128\t\n   129\t**Purpose:** Where to return after completing the current evaluation. Enables pausable, resumable computation.\n   130\t\n   131\t**Structure:**\n   132\t```clojure\n   133\t{:frame  <ast-node>          ; The expression that's waiting for a value\n   105\t  `effect-forgery-test` = 48 tests/521 assertions green; `engine/ast-walker/\n   106\t  semantic-engine/debruijn-register-effects/parity/rule-r/mint/yin.vm` = 146/1492 green;\n   107\t  debruijn stack+register lanes = 99/843 green; semantic suite (vm/effects/code/parity/\n   108\t  frame/linearize) = 125/2339 green. All on the fbd8da0f tree. 521 tests / 6188\n   109\t  assertions total beyond the battery — zero failures.\n   110\t- **Snapshot semantics**: `telemetry/emit-snapshot` snapshots state wholesale; GC keeps\n   111\t  whole entries (P13 proves retention across a collection). Heap is task state, not\n   112\t  continuation state — re-entry semantics unchanged.\n   113\t- **`:cell/new-retained`** is instruction-for-instruction the `:cell/new` arm\n   114\t  (allocation counting, `gensym`, `issue-ref`, same seal derivation); only the write\n   115\t  carries the mark. `:cell/retained?` mirrors `:cell/authentic?` exactly (pure, never\n   116\t  fatal). Both are additive `case` arms before the unknown-effect fallback.\n   117\t\n   118\t### 2. `:cell/set!` refusal — safe as a general rule\n   119\t\n   120\tThe refusal is scoped by construction, not by policy: ONLY the retained mint writes the\n   121\tmark, ONLY `dsg__condition_wrapper` (compiler prelude, reserved-prefix binding) calls\n   122\tthe mint, and the wrapper is written exactly once at mint. `heap-write`'s new\n   123\tmark-preservation clause is therefore currently unreachable (a marked cell can never\n   124\treach a set!) — dead but harmless, and the right invariant if a second marked kind ever\n   125\tappears. Unmarked guest cells are unaffected (P11). Fail-closed shape matches\n   126\t`check-ref!`'s convention (`:retained-cell` names reason+effect+id).\n   127\t\n ...76-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-master-green-recovery.md |  24 ++\n ...ode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-seat-takeover.md | 311 +++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 335 insertions(+)\n0326a044 test(yang.call): the provenance forgery contract pins — RED pending the VM provenance primitive (owner-authorized)\n test/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj | 77 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 77 insertions(+)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
